UPDATE companies SET description='Rogers Electrical Contracting Company, Inc. was founded in 1996 and is headquartered in Fairmont, West Virginia. The firm operates additional divisions in Pennsylvania, Illinois, and North Carolina to serve industrial and commercial customers across the region.

The company provides turnkey electrical contracting services encompassing engineering and design, power line and substation construction, system automation and PLC/SCADA integration, control panel fabrication, fiber optic installation and testing, commercial electrical systems, and bore hole cable services for mining applications. Its in-house professional engineer and design team use CAD, ETAP, and PLS-CADD software to produce detailed project renderings, while an extensive equipment fleet enables work at remote job sites.

Rogers Electrical serves the aggregate, oil and gas, coal, water, and electric utility industries, as well as commercial construction. Notable projects include a turnkey upgrade of a coal preparation plant in Philippi, WV, involving electrical design, installation, programming, and start-up, and the design and build of a 50 MVA 138-34.5 kV substation for a mine power system in the same area.

The firm emphasizes its more than three decades of industry experience and a commitment to going the extra mile for quality. Its service model combines complete plant builds, plant upgrades, overland conveyor systems, motor control centers, and PLC programming under a single turnkey umbrella, aiming to make projects efficient and cost-effective.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Engineering/Design Services (CAD, ETAP, PLS-CADD)", "Power Line Construction", "Substation Construction", "System Automation & PLC/SCADA Integration", "PLC Control Panel Design/Build", "Fiber Optic Installation & Testing", "Commercial Electrical Systems", "Electrical System Installation & Maintenance (medium/high voltage, MCC, switchgear, VFDs, transformers)", "Networking/Wireless Communication Systems (Fiber, Ethernet, Wireless, Mesh, Cellular, Satellite)", "Bore Hole Cable Services (lowering/retrieving mining cable, cable repair, vulcanizing)", "Off-Grid Power Solutions", "Grounding & Lightning Protection", "Overland Conveyor System Electrical", "Motor Control Center (MCC) Installation", "PLC Programming"], "industries": ["Aggregate", "Oil and Gas", "Coal Mining", "Water/Wastewater", "Electric Utility", "Commercial Construction", "Industrial Manufacturing"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Bore Hole Truck"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Turnkey electrical system design, automation, and installation", "In-house professional engineer and design team using CAD, ETAP, PLS-CADD", "Extensive equipment fleet for remote job site access", "Over 30 years of experience across aggregate, coal, utility, and water sectors", "Single-source responsibility for plant builds, upgrades, and conveyor systems"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1996 -> db", "Headquartered in Fairmont, WV -> /about", "Divisions in Pennsylvania, Illinois, North Carolina -> /about", "Turnkey electrical contracting services -> /", "Engineering/design with CAD, ETAP, PLS-CADD -> /services", "Power line and substation construction -> /services", "System automation and PLC/SCADA integration -> /services", "Control panel design/build -> /services", "Fiber optic installation and testing -> /services", "Bore hole cable services for mining -> /services", "Industries: aggregate, oil and gas, coal, water, electric utility -> /about", "Project: Major Coal Plant Upgrade, Philippi, WV -> /", "Project: Mine Power System with 50 MVA substation, Philippi, WV -> /", "Management team includes Mark Dalton (President, PE), Ryan Erdie, Charles Pratt, Jerry Tucker, David Dudash, Ian Frailey, Craig Rogers, Brian Bulatko, Jason Tomaro -> /about", "Over 30 years industry experience -> /about", "Extensive equipment fleet for remote sites -> /services", "In-house professional engineer -> /services", "State Fire Marshal and MSHA certifications held by staff -> /about"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Rogers Electrical is an electrical contracting company the specializes in Turn-Key electrical projects for various industrial and commercial customers.", "founded_year": "1996", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/rogers-electrical-contracting-company-inc/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='rogers-electrical-contracting' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Ron''s Home Style Foods was founded in the spring of 1985 by Ron Woodall in Houston, Texas. The family-owned company began with a mission to produce high-quality, home-style deli salads that look and taste homemade. Woodall had previously developed the successful Ron''s Krispy Fried Chicken chain before launching the venture.

Today the company operates a USDA- and FDA-inspected production facility where it makes deli salads, dips and spreads, dressings and bases, gourmet burger kits, frozen sides and entrees, and provides co-packing and private-label services. Products are prepared fresh daily using high-quality ingredients, and the facility is described as exceeding food-safety expectations.

Ron''s serves the foodservice and grocery channels nationwide. Its retail line, Texas Kitchen, is stocked in major Texas chains including Brookshire Brothers, H-E-B, and Kroger. The company also partners with foodservice distributors and recently announced a collaboration with Center of the Plate Foods Sales to accelerate national growth.

The business emphasizes a homemade look and taste, with attention to detail that extends beyond what can be seen and tasted. Its founding goal remains the benchmark: delivering products that meet global food-safety standards while satisfying customer expectations for quality and consistency.', certifications=ARRAY['USDA inspection','FDA inspection']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Deli Salads", "Dips & Spreads", "Dressings & Bases", "Gourmet Burger Kits", "Frozen Sides & Entrees", "Co-Packing", "Private Labeling"], "industries": ["Foodservice", "Grocery"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Fresh daily production under USDA and FDA inspection", "Facility exceeds food-safety expectations", "Family-owned and operated since 1985", "Co-packing and private-label services", "Retail distribution through major Texas chains (HEB, Kroger, Brookshire Brothers)"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1985 -> db", "Founder Ron Woodall -> /", "Headquarters Houston, Texas -> db, /", "Family-owned -> /", "Products: Deli Salads, Dips & Spreads, Dressings & Bases, Gourmet Burger Kits, Frozen Sides & Entrees, Co-Packing, Private Labeling -> db", "Processes: fresh daily under USDA and FDA inspection -> /", "Industries: Foodservice, Grocery -> db", "Customers: Brookshire Brothers, HEB, Kroger -> /", "Retail line: Texas Kitchen -> /", "Partnership with Center of the Plate Foods Sales -> /", "Certifications: USDA and FDA inspection -> /", "Mission: create high-quality home-style deli salads -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "a distinguished family-owned food manufacturer specializing in freshly prepared foods", "founded_year": "1985", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='ron-s-home-style-foods' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Rooftop Power is a family-owned solar and roofing company headquartered in Warwick, Rhode Island, founded in 2017. The business began with a focus on helping homeowners across Rhode Island, Massachusetts, and Connecticut reduce their electric bills through rooftop solar.

The company installs custom residential and commercial solar arrays, integrates battery storage, standby generators, and EV chargers, and provides roofing replacement and repair—all performed by its own electricians, roofers, and installers.

Its customers are primarily single-family homeowners and commercial building owners in Rhode Island, Massachusetts, and Connecticut who want to lower energy costs, gain backup power, or combine a roof replacement with solar. The firm also services orphaned systems originally installed by other contractors.

Rooftop Power was built to eliminate the coordination gaps that arise when solar, roofing, and electrical work are split among multiple contractors. It offers a single workmanship warranty covering both roof and array, one project manager and schedule, and a single point of contact for service calls years after installation.', certifications=ARRAY['BBB A+ Accredited','Rhode Island Electrical License AC004027','Massachusetts Electrical License','Connecticut Electrical License','Tesla Powerwall Certified Installer']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Residential solar design and installation", "Commercial solar design and installation", "Battery storage system installation (Tesla Powerwall)", "Standby generator installation", "EV charger installation (Level 2)", "Roof replacement and repair", "Solar system removal and reinstallation", "Solar system maintenance and repair", "System add-ons and expansions", "Electrical panel upgrades", "Permitting and utility interconnection management", "Engineering and production modeling", "Site survey and structural assessment", "Energy consumption analysis and bill review", "Net metering and incentive program enrollment (REG, REF, SMART)"], "industries": ["Residential solar", "Commercial solar", "Roofing", "Energy storage", "Backup power generation", "Electric vehicle charging", "Renewable energy incentives consulting"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Tesla Powerwall"], "volume": "4,000+ projects (19,125 kW installed)", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house crews (electricians, roofers, installers) rather than subcontractors", "Single workmanship warranty covering roof and solar together", "One project manager, one schedule, one permit and utility interconnection process", "Services and warranties systems installed by any other company", "Tesla Powerwall certified installer"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2017 -> db", "Family-owned -> db description", "Headquarters Warwick, RI -> db hq_city/hq_state", "4,000+ projects -> page ''/''", "19,125 kW installed -> page ''/''", "Licensed in RI, MA, CT -> page ''/services''", "BBB A+ Accredited -> page ''/''", "Tesla Powerwall certified -> page ''/services''", "In-house crews not subcontractors -> page ''/services''", "Single workmanship warranty covering roof and solar -> page ''/services''", "Services systems from any installer -> page ''/services''", "Residential and commercial solar installation -> page ''/services''", "Roof replacement and repair -> page ''/services''", "Battery storage installation -> page ''/services''", "Standby generator installation -> page ''/services''", "EV charger installation -> page ''/services''", "Removal/reinstallation -> page ''/services''", "Maintenance/service -> page ''/services''", "System add-ons -> page ''/services''", "Permitting and utility interconnection handled -> page ''/services''", "Engineering and design -> page ''/services''", "Site survey -> page ''/services''", "Four payment options (Loan, Cash, PPA, Lease) -> page ''/''", "Net metering and incentive programs (REG, REF, SMART) -> page ''/''"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We are a solar company and a roofing company and a licensed electrical contractor under one roof, with our own crews doing the work.", "founded_year": "2017", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='rooftop-power' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Rooftop Solar is based in Phoenix, Arizona, and was founded in 1979. The company was co-founded by Hadassah, who serves as its chief operating officer. Hadassah’s background in urban and environmental planning included managing a land conservation collaborative spanning more than 425,000 acres before she developed the expertise to launch a solar installation business.

The firm designs and installs custom photovoltaic systems for homes and businesses across the Phoenix metropolitan area, including Anthem, Cave Creek, Mesa, Chandler, Goodyear, Glendale, and Scottsdale. It partners exclusively with manufacturers such as REC, LG, Panasonic, Hanwha, Solaria, Enphase, SolarEdge, and Tesla Powerwall for modules, inverters, and storage. Rooftop Solar holds NABCEP certification along with Arizona electrical and dual building contractor licenses, and it backs every installation with a third-party 30-year warranty covering equipment, roofing, and labor. Financing is arranged through credit-union partnerships that eliminate dealer fees.

Customers range from individual homeowners to schools, churches, hospitals, historic buildings, multifamily housing, hotels, and office towers. Commercial projects include solar carports, parking canopies, rooftop arrays, and ground-mount systems. The company also assists clients with tax incentives, rebates, and accelerated depreciation strategies.

Hadassah’s founding vision was rooted in the belief that everyone deserves a healthy environment and a bright energy future. Rooftop Solar emphasizes a low-pressure, educational sales approach and a customer experience that extends throughout the system’s lifespan, supported by a dedicated service department.', certifications=ARRAY['NABCEP Certification','Arizona Electrical Contractor License','Arizona Dual Building Contractor License','Licensed and Bonded (Arizona)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Residential solar panel installation", "Commercial solar panel installation", "Custom solar system design", "Solar carport and parking canopy installation", "Rooftop and ground-mount solar installation", "Energy storage system installation (Tesla Powerwall)", "Solar financing and leasing arrangement", "Solar tax incentive and rebate consultation", "Solar system maintenance and service", "Third-party 30-year warranty administration"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Education", "Religious institutions", "Healthcare", "Historic buildings", "Multifamily housing", "Hospitality", "Commercial office"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Exclusive third-party 30-year equipment, roofing, and labor warranty", "NABCEP certified with Arizona electrical and dual building contractor licenses", "Exclusive credit union financing partnerships with no dealer fees", "Over 10 years of Phoenix-area experience with roofing background", "Exclusive partnerships with top-tier solar manufacturers (REC, LG, Panasonic, Hanwha, Solaria, Enphase, SolarEdge)"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1979 -> db", "Headquartered in Phoenix, Arizona -> db", "Hadassah co-founded Rooftop Solar and serves as COO -> db", "Over 10 years of local Phoenix experience with roofing background -> /", "Licensed, bonded, NABCEP certified with electrical and dual building contractor licenses -> /", "Exclusive 30-year equipment, roofing, and labor warranty -> /", "Partners exclusively with REC, LG, Panasonic, Hanwha, Solaria, Enphase, SolarEdge, Tesla Powerwall -> /", "Offers residential and commercial solar installation including carports, rooftop, ground mounts -> /", "Serves Phoenix metro area: Anthem, Cave Creek, Mesa, Chandler, Goodyear, Glendale, Scottsdale -> /", "Provides financing through credit unions with no dealer fees -> /", "Installs for hospitals, historic buildings, multifamily housing, hotels, office buildings, schools, churches -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Rooftop Solar is licensed, bonded, NABCEP certified with electrical and dual building contractor licenses.", "founded_year": "1979", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='rooftop-solar' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Rooted Furniture operates from a workshop in Boulder, Colorado, where it designs and builds custom solid-wood furniture. The company was established to create heirloom-quality pieces using only sustainably harvested North American hardwoods, avoiding plywood and veneer entirely.

Each piece is handcrafted from domestically sourced species such as white oak, black walnut, hard maple, and cherry. The shop employs traditional joinery techniques — mortise and tenon, dovetail, and tongue and groove — and finishes every surface with a plant-based, non-toxic oil that is food-safe and VOC-free. Projects typically move from consultation to delivery in eight to fourteen weeks, depending on complexity.

Rooted serves residential clients across the Front Range and ships nationwide via white-glove freight carriers.

A core differentiator is the Planting Roots initiative, which plants a tree through the National Forest Foundation for every table sold. The business emphasizes responsible forestry, using FSC-certified, ECC, CARB, and LEED-compliant lumber, and invites customers to visit its Boulder workshop by appointment.', certifications=ARRAY['FSC certified','ECC compliant','CARB compliant','LEED compliant']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture design and consultation", "Traditional joinery (mortise and tenon, dovetail, tongue and groove)", "Hand selection of lumber", "Plant-based oil finishing", "White-glove delivery and installation", "Workshop visits by appointment", "Custom commissions for residential and commercial clients"], "industries": ["Residential furniture", "Custom furniture", "Office furniture", "Gift and accessory items"], "materials": ["White oak", "Black walnut", "Hard maple", "Cherry", "North American oak"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "8-14 weeks for custom pieces", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Handcrafted solid hardwood construction with traditional joinery", "Plant-based, non-toxic, food-safe finish on all pieces", "Sustainably harvested domestic hardwoods (FSC, ECC, CARB, LEED compliant)", "Tree planted for every table sold via National Forest Foundation", "Custom design-to-delivery in 8\u201314 weeks"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Boulder, Colorado -> db", "Handmade solid hardwood furniture, no plywood or veneer -> /", "Uses sustainably harvested North American oak, white oak, black walnut, hard maple, cherry -> /", "Traditional joinery techniques: mortise and tenon, dovetail, tongue and groove -> /", "Plant-based, non-toxic, food-safe finish -> /", "Lead time 8-14 weeks from consultation to delivery -> /", "Ships nationwide, local delivery in Front Range -> /", "Plants a tree for every table sold via National Forest Foundation -> /", "Workshop in Boulder open for visits by appointment -> /", "Wood certifications: FSC, ECC, CARB, LEED compliant -> /", "Serves residential and office clients -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Every piece of furniture from Rooted is handcrafted from the finest solid hardwood.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='rooted-furniture' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Rosebud Wood Products was founded in 1965 in Madison, South Dakota, as a family-owned cabinetry shop. The company began producing semi-custom and custom kitchen and bath cabinetry for residential customers, building a reputation for quality craftsmanship.

Today the firm operates a 62,000-square-foot manufacturing facility in Madison, where it produces a range of cabinetry lines including the Supreme and Traditional series, multi-family SMART cabinetry, commercial casework, hospitality furniture, and closet systems. The workforce includes multiple generations of employees, many with decades of tenure, though the company does not disclose an exact headcount.

Rosebud serves residential, commercial, multifamily, and hospitality markets across the Midwest and beyond, with showrooms in Madison, the Sioux Falls area, and Dickinson, North Dakota. Its customer base includes homeowners, designers, builders, and hospitality operators seeking tailored wood products for kitchens, baths, offices, entertainment centers, fireplaces, and closets.

The company emphasizes flexibility, offering made-to-order modifications to its standard cabinet lines and providing free design services using current cabinet design software. Its culture centers on combining innovative processes with the experience of long-tenured employees, reflecting a belief that quality pays rather than costs.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Semi-custom cabinetry manufacturing", "Custom cabinetry manufacturing", "Case goods manufacturing", "Wood component manufacturing", "Hospitality furniture manufacturing", "Closet systems manufacturing", "Commercial casework and woodwork", "Multi-family cabinetry (SMART Cabinetry)", "Cabinet design services", "Cabinet modification services"], "industries": ["Residential kitchen and bath", "Hospitality furniture", "Commercial casework", "Multifamily housing", "Office and entertainment", "Closet systems"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Modifies Traditional and Supreme cabinet lines for semi-custom and custom orders", "Free design services using latest cabinet design software", "62,000 sq ft manufacturing facility in Madison, SD", "Family-owned with multi-generational workforce", "Quality culture combining innovative processes with experienced employees"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1965 -> db", "Headquarters Madison, SD -> db", "Family owned and operated -> /about", "62,000 sq ft manufacturing facility -> /about", "Expanded into hospitality furniture in 1985 -> db", "Many employees 20+ years -> /about", "Offers Supreme Series, Traditional Series, SMART Cabinetry, Commercial Casework, Hospitality Furniture, Closet Systems -> /about", "Free design services using latest cabinet design software -> /", "Flexibility to modify Traditional or Supreme lines -> /", "Showrooms in Madison SD, Sioux Falls area, Dickinson ND -> /about", "Quality culture combining innovative processes with experienced employees -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our 62,000 square foot manufacturing facility is currently located in the small town of Madison, South Dakota.", "founded_year": "1965", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='rosebud-wood-products' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Route 66 Controls LLC was founded in 2005 in Cuba, Missouri, by Dr. Pourya Shamsi, who serves as CEO and lead design engineer. The company is structured as a design-engineer-owned firm, with its principal engineers holding ownership stakes, a model the firm says keeps overhead low and aligns incentives with project outcomes.

The firm provides end-to-end R&D for power electronics and motor drives, covering electrical and mechanical design, finite-element simulation, embedded software development, prototyping, and testing. Its engineers work with tools such as Altium, Ansys, Matlab, and SolidWorks to deliver custom converters up to 2 MW, 2,000 A, and 12 kV, and can prototype systems up to 5 MW at IP68 ratings. In-house test capacity reaches 500 kW for converters and 300 kW for drives, supplemented by a local machining partner for larger mechanical structures. The company produces hundreds of prototypes annually but does not pursue high-volume manufacturing.

Customers span aerospace (ground-support and onboard chargers), automotive (traction drives), industrial UPS, and emerging airship and eVTOL platforms. A noted reference project is the energy-management and battery-charger system powering LTA''s airship. The firm also serves startups needing low-cost prototypes for fundraising and established OEMs seeking manufacturing-ready designs for certification.

Route 66 Controls differentiates itself through full intellectual-property transfer — including design files, code, patents, and training — under NDA protection. Its PhD-level engineers, many of whom hold university faculty positions, bring federally funded research experience (NSF, DOE, DoD) to commercial projects, targeting delivery within three to six months.', certifications=ARRAY['UL1741 (hardware)','UL1998 (software safety)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electrical design (hardware, software, system integration)", "Mechanical design (SolidWorks, Fusion 360)", "Finite element analysis (Ansys FEM, IcePak thermal)", "Simulation (Matlab)", "Control design (digital control, RTOS programming)", "Motor drives design", "Power electronics design", "Magnetics design", "Thermal design and analysis", "Wide bandgap technologies (SiC, GaN)", "Prototyping (electrical and mechanical, up to 5 MW, IP68)", "Low-volume manufacturing", "Testing (up to 500 kW converters, 300 kW drives)", "Tech transfer (training, documentation, full design file transfer)", "Idea development and patentable design conceptualization", "Embedded software coding (RTOS)", "Compliance with UL1741, UL1998, SIL 3/ASIL-D", "Local machining partner for larger mechanical structures", "On-site deployment support"], "industries": ["Aerospace (ground support, onboard chargers/drives)", "Automotive (traction drives)", "Industrial (UPS systems)", "Airship (LTA airship energy management)", "Transportation electrification (eVTOL)", "Battery charging systems", "Motor drives", "Power conversion", "Renewable energy (medium voltage DFIG drives)"], "materials": ["Silicon Carbide (SiC) semiconductors", "Gallium Nitride (GaN) semiconductors"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Hundreds of prototypes per year up to 5 MW; not large-scale manufacturing", "lead_time": "3-6 months for design projects", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Design-engineer-owned structure with lead engineers as shareholders", "Full IP rights transfer including design files, code, patents, and training", "PhD design engineers with university faculty roles and federal research funding", "In-house testing up to 500 kW (converters) and 300 kW (drives)", "Prototyping capability up to 5 MW and IP68 environmental rating"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2005 in Cuba, Missouri -> db", "Design-engineer-owned firm with lead engineers as owners -> /services", "CEO Dr. Pourya Shamsi with 20 years experience, top 2% researcher -> /services", "Services: electrical/mechanical design, simulation, prototyping, testing, tech transfer -> /services", "Custom converters up to 2MW, 2000A, 12kV -> /", "Testing capacity 500kW converters, 300kW drives -> /services", "Prototyping up to 5MW, IP68 rating -> /services", "Hundreds of prototypes per year, not large-scale manufacturing -> /services", "Industries: aerospace, automotive, industrial UPS, airship (LTA), eVTOL -> /, /services", "Full IP transfer including design files, code, patents, training under NDA -> /", "PhD engineers, university faculty, federal funding (NSF, DOE, DoD) -> /services", "Target delivery 3-6 months -> /", "Software tools: Altium, Eagle, Ansys, Matlab, SolidWorks, Fusion 360 -> /services", "Standards: UL1741, UL1998, SIL 3/ASIL-D -> /services", "Local machining partner for larger mechanical structures -> /services", "Wide bandgap technologies (SiC, GaN) -> /services", "Products: XM3 Module Gate Drivers, 3/5 Phase Inverters -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Even though we can develop hundreds of prototypes of up to ~5MW per year, we are not poised for large scale manufacturing.", "founded_year": "2005", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='route-66-controls-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Rubix Foods traces its roots to Jacksonville, Florida, where Aaron Block and Aaron Lapin co-founded Reddi-Wip in 1948. The business evolved through the Block family for five generations, with Mickey Block building the first U.S. ultra-high-temperature dairy plant in 1965. Darifair Foods was established in 1981 as the first national dairy supplier, becoming the nation’s largest producer of portion-controlled private-label sour cream by the 1990s. In 2021 the company rebranded as Rubix Foods, expanding beyond dairy into end-to-end product development under continued family ownership.

Today Rubix operates as a full-service product development house with end-to-end manufacturing capabilities. Its 50,000-square-foot Innovation Center, opened in 2022 and FDA-registered in 2024, houses R&D, culinary, and production under one roof. Core platforms include compound butter systems, sauces and glazes, dips/spreads/fillings, performance blends, marination systems, aerosol systems, cultured dairy (sour creams, yogurts), and dairy essentials such as milk, buttermilk, and cream. The facility supports custom formulation from concept through commercialization.

Rubix positions itself on speed, quality, and reliability, aiming to be the industry’s first call for solving tough formulation challenges. Its NEXT Flavor Network leverages Gen Z social-media creators to deliver real-time consumer insights, while a disciplined “velocity to market” approach compresses development timelines without sacrificing execution.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Compound Butter Systems", "Sauces & Glazes", "Dips, Spreads and Fillings", "Performance Blends", "Marination Systems", "Aerosol Systems", "Sour Creams & Yogurts", "Dairy Essentials", "Product Development"], "industries": ["Foodservice", "Food manufacturing"], "materials": ["Butter", "Cream", "Milk", "Buttermilk", "Sour cream", "Yogurt", "Cheese"], "equipment": ["HTST skid rig", "UHT dairy plant"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Full-service product development with end-to-end manufacturing under one roof", "50,000 sq ft FDA-registered Innovation Center combining R&D and production", "Proprietary Gen Z consumer insights via the NEXT Flavor Network", "Velocity-to-market model emphasizing disciplined, intentional speed", "Five-generation family ownership providing continuity and deep dairy expertise"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1981 as Darifair Foods -> /about", "Headquarters in Jacksonville, Florida -> /about", "Family-owned across five generations (Block family) -> /about", "50,000 sq ft Innovation Center opened 2022 -> /about", "FDA-registered food manufacturing status achieved 2024 -> /about", "Capabilities include Compound Butter Systems, Sauces & Glazes, Dips/Spreads/Fillings, Performance Blends, Marination Systems, Aerosol Systems, Sour Creams & Yogurts, Dairy Essentials, Product Development -> /capabilities", "Industries served: Foodservice -> db", "HTST skid rig invested 2005 -> /about", "UHT dairy plant built 1965 -> /about", "Reddi-Wip co-founded 1948 in Jacksonville -> /about", "Rebranded to Rubix Foods 2021 -> /about", "Arbor Investments partnership 2019 and reinvestment 2025 -> /about", "Ryan Smith named CEO 2025 -> /about", "NEXT Flavor Network provides proprietary Gen Z consumer insights -> /", "Full-service product development with end-to-end manufacturing -> /about", "Velocity to market with disciplined execution -> /capabilities"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Rubix Foods is a full-service product development house with end-to-end manufacturing capabilities.", "founded_year": "1981", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='rubix-foods' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Ryone Manufacturing Company, based in North Providence, Rhode Island, has been producing precision cutting tools since 1972. The company was founded by Arthur "Garfield" Ryone and remains under family ownership, with the Ryone family collectively bringing over 100 years of experience to the operation.

The shop specializes in regrinding and roll grinding services, handling roll grinding up to 20-inch diameter and 80-inch length, and offers a full range of machine shop capabilities. These include CNC turning with live tooling up to 12 inches, CNC vertical milling up to 18 by 36 inches, OD grinding up to 20-inch diameter, rotary grinding up to 16-inch diameter, and turning up to 22-inch diameter. The company also manufactures custom saw blades, slitting knives, and special shank tools in both steel and carbide, and provides full re-sharpening services for those materials.

Ryone serves the metal and plastic industries, supplying cutting tools and machined components to customers who require precision grinding and custom tooling. The business works from customer prints for custom parts and caters to orders for regrinding and resharpening of existing tools.

