UPDATE companies SET description='SAVKAT was founded in 2017 in Bristol, Connecticut, by Steve Salansky, who named the company after his daughter Savannah Kathryn. The business began as a family-owned venture in West Hartford before expanding to serve greater New England, with a mission to make premium renewable energy systems accessible to homeowners.

The company provides complete home energy and protection services, including solar energy system design and installation, GAF-certified roofing, battery backup (FranklinWH, Tesla Powerwall, Enphase), EV charging, and solar panel removal and reinstallation. All work is performed by in-house crews—sales, engineering, permitting, installation, and service—without subcontractors. SAVKAT has completed over 3,500 residential installations and offers a 25-year comprehensive warranty.

SAVKAT serves residential homeowners across Connecticut and greater New England, helping them achieve energy independence through solar, storage, and roofing solutions. The company also works with customers seeking battery backup for grid resilience and EV charging integration. Its technology-agnostic approach means it selects equipment from brands such as Enphase, FranklinWH, REC, Qcells, and SolarEdge based on each home''s needs.

Salansky founded SAVKAT to offer a local alternative to national solar chains that rely on subcontractors and distant call centers. The company emphasizes accountability: one team, one warranty, one phone number, and crews that are direct employees. It also leverages nearby warehousing for faster material delivery and quicker installations.', certifications=ARRAY['CT HIC Licensed #0648178','GAF Certified Roofer','Elite Enphase Partner']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar energy system design and installation", "Roofing installation (GAF certified)", "Battery backup system installation (FranklinWH, Tesla Powerwall, Enphase)", "EV charging station installation (Level 2)", "Solar panel removal and reinstallation", "Energy consulting and custom system design", "Permitting and utility coordination", "Project management", "In-house installation crews (electricians and installers)", "Post-installation monitoring and service"], "industries": ["Residential solar", "Roofing", "Energy storage", "EV charging infrastructure", "Home energy services", "Renewable energy"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house crews for all installations (no subcontractors)", "25-year comprehensive warranty covering all services", "Local Connecticut-based team with direct phone access", "Technology-agnostic product selection from multiple premium brands", "Single point of contact for sales, engineering, installation, and service"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2017 by Steve Salansky -> /", "Named after daughter Savannah Kathryn -> /", "Headquarters in Bristol, CT -> db", "Family-owned since 2017 -> /", "In-house crews, no subcontractors -> /", "3,500+ installations completed -> /", "25-year comprehensive warranty -> /", "CT HIC Licensed #0648178 -> /", "GAF Certified Roofer -> /", "Elite Enphase Partner -> /", "Services: solar, roofing, battery, EV charging, panel removal -> /", "Brands: Enphase, FranklinWH, Tesla Powerwall, REC, Qcells, Pegasus, Maxeon, SolarEdge -> /about", "Founded by Steven Salansky and Liz Karnuk in West Hartford, CT -> /about", "1204+ homes converted to solar -> /about", "55000+ metric tons CO2 saved -> /about", "In-house team includes solar consultants, project managers, electricians, installers -> /about", "Warehoused nearby for faster transit -> /about"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "One team handles everything\u2014sales, engineering, installation, and service. No subcontractors on your roof.", "founded_year": "2017", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/savkatinc/"], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='savkat' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='SEA Wire and Cable, Inc. is headquartered in Madison, Alabama. The company traces its roots to 1970 when Gary Griffin founded South Eastern Associates as a manufacturer''s representative firm. In 1982 the business was incorporated as SEA Wire and Cable and shifted its focus to stocking and distributing military-specification wire and cable. The operation moved to the Madison area in 1977 and expanded its warehouse and office space several times through the 1980s. In the early 2000s the company became a small woman-owned business when Griffin transferred ownership to his daughter, Dana Town, who continues to lead the firm.

The company maintains an 80,000-square-foot facility stocked with more than 15,000 line items and over 80 million feet of wire. Beyond distribution, SEA provides value-added services including laser wire marking, custom color coding, dyeing, cut-and-strip operations, planetary twisting, kitting, sub-assembly, and a suite of electrical tests such as hipot, spark, pull and solderability checks. It also manages customer inventory through Kanban, just-in-time, dock-to-stock, consignment and other programs, and ships in-stock orders the same day.

The customer base spans military, aerospace and commercial sectors, with named accounts that include Boeing, Unison Industries and Lockheed Martin. SEA''s quality system is certified to AS9100 and ISO 9001, and the company emphasizes full traceability back to the original manufacturer, retaining certificates of conformance and test reports for every lot.

SEA''s stated mission is to take care of its customers, partners, employees, stakeholders and the warfighter "one connection at a time." Its core values — Service, Excellence, Accountability — underpin a quality program that targets zero defects through comprehensive incoming inspection and root-cause corrective action.', certifications=ARRAY['AS9100','ISO 9001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Laser wire marking", "Custom color coding", "Custom labeling", "Dyeing", "Cut and strip wire", "Planetary twisting", "Cut and marked tubing", "Etching", "Kitting", "Sub-assembly", "Hipot testing (resistance, leakage, breakdown)", "Spark testing", "Pull testing", "Solderability testing", "Inventory management (Kanban, JIT, dock-to-stock, demand-pull, consignment, stock rotation)", "EDI (X12 standard)", "Barcode scanning for dock-to-stock", "Automated sales desk and real-time networked system", "Online UPS/FedEx tracking"], "industries": ["Military", "Aerospace", "Commercial", "Defense"], "materials": ["M22759 wire", "M27500 cable", "M23053 heat shrink tubing", "EMI/RFI backshells", "Connector backshells (Isodyne)"], "equipment": ["Prophet 21 ERP system"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Same-day shipping for in-stock items", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Same-day shipping on in-stock items", "Full traceability with factory test reports and certificates of conformance", "Over 15,000 SKUs and 80+ million feet of wire in a single 80,000-sq-ft facility", "Value-added services including laser marking, custom cables, kitting and inventory management programs", "AS9100/ISO 9001 certified quality system with dedicated incoming inspection"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1970 as South Eastern Associates by Gary Griffin -> /about-us", "Became SEA Wire and Cable Inc. in 1982 -> /about-us", "Moved to Madison, AL area in 1977 -> /about-us", "Woman-owned since early 2000s, passed to Dana Town -> /about-us", "Stocks over 15,000 items and 80 million+ feet of wire in 80,000 sq ft facility -> /abo