UPDATE companies SET description='SINTX Technologies operates from Salt Lake City, Utah, where it was founded in 1996. The company is publicly traded on the NASDAQ under the ticker SINT. Its origins trace back to the development of technical ceramic and composite components for biomedical, aerospace, defense, and energy markets, with a focus on silicon nitride innovation since its inception.

The company manufactures silicon nitride and other advanced ceramics, controlling the entire process in-house from powder preparation through final inspection. Capabilities include powder preparation, mechanical and isostatic dry pressing, green machining with up to 5-axis capability, debinding, sintering, hot isostatic pressing, and quality control. An R&D cell supports compounding, extrusion, and 3D printing of silicon nitride-containing polymer composites, while an R&D lab provides powder characterization, microscopy, and pathogen testing. The FDA- and ANVISA-registered facility serves prototype to production volumes.

SINTX serves biomedical, aerospace, defense, and energy sectors. In the biomedical space, it produces silicon nitride spinal implants and hip/knee prosthetic components with demonstrated antibacterial and osseointegrative properties. Its FleX SN-AP antipathogenic powder is being evaluated as an additive or coating for medical and non-medical products. The company has also secured a supply agreement with Evonik to manufacture a silicon nitride–PEEK compound for AI-assisted, 3D-printed parts.

SINTX distinguishes itself as one of the few firms capable of manufacturing silicon nitride products completely in-house for medical devices. Full control over powder preparation enables tailored material properties, and private-label partnerships allow customers to leverage validated designs under their own brands.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 13485:2016','AS9100D','FDA registered facility','ANVISA registered facility']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Powder preparation", "Dry pressing (mechanical and isostatic)", "Green machining (up to 5-axis)", "Debinding", "Sintering", "Hot isostatic pressing", "Quality control", "Compounding", "Extrusion", "3D printing of silicon nitride-containing polymer composites", "Powder characterization", "Microscopy and image analysis", "Pathogen testing", "Private label manufacturing"], "industries": ["Biomedical", "Aerospace", "Defense", "Energy", "Antipathogenic/antimicrobial applications"], "materials": ["Silicon nitride (Si3N4)", "Silicon nitride\u2013PEEK compound", "FleX SN-AP antipathogenic powder", "Advanced ceramics"], "equipment": ["5-axis machining centers", "Debinding, sintering, and hot isostatic pressing furnaces", "Laser for implant texturing", "Compounding and extrusion equipment", "3D printers for polymer-ceramic composites", "High-resolution microscopes with image processing", "Pathogen testing cell"], "volume": "Prototype to production levels", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["One of few companies manufacturing silicon nitride products completely in-house for medical devices", "Full control of silicon nitride manufacturing process from powder preparation", "FDA and ANVISA registered facility with ISO 13485:2016 and AS9100D certification", "Publicly traded on NASDAQ (SINT)", "Private label partnerships for accelerated market access"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1996 -> db", "Headquarters Salt Lake City, Utah -> db", "Manufacturer of silicon nitride and advanced ceramics -> /", "Innovating with silicon nitride since 1996 -> /", "Expanded to other advanced ceramics in 2021 -> /", "Biomedical applications: spinal implants, hip/knee prosthetics -> /", "Antipathogenic powder FleX SN-AP -> /", "Supply agreement with Evonik for silicon nitride-PEEK compound -> /", "FDA and ANVISA registered manufacturing facility -> /about", "ISO 13485:2016 and AS9100D certified -> /about", "Publicly traded on NASDAQ (SINT) -> /about", "Processes: powder preparation, dry pressing, green machining (5-axis), debinding, sintering, HIP, quality control -> /about", "R&D cell: compounding, extrusion, 3D printing of silicon nitride-polymer composites -> /about", "R&D lab: powder characterization, microscopy, pathogen testing -> /about", "Laser for texturing spinal implants -> /about", "Private label options -> /about", "Industries: biomedical, aerospace, defense, energy -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "SINTX is a leading manufacturer of silicon nitride and other advanced ceramics.", "founded_year": "1996", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sintx-technologies' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='SML Packaging Solutions, LLC was founded in 2005 in the Lynchburg, Virginia area and is now headquartered in Forest, Virginia. The company was established to design and build custom packing machinery for the glass and plastic bottling industry, drawing on what it describes as more than 150 years of combined engineering expertise among its team.

The company manufactures a line of case packers and inspection equipment, including the Glass House Packer, Drop Case Packer, Small Brewery Case Packer, Variety Pack Line, and Case Checker, along with drop grids and clamps compatible with major case packers. The Drop Case Packer is rated at up to 30 cases per minute (43,200 bottles per hour) and handles glass or plastic bottles and jars of various shapes. The Small Brewery Case Packer operates at 30 to 350 bottles per minute in a compact footprint suited for tight spaces. All machines are designed for 24/7 operation and can be customized for specific bottle sizes, pack configurations, and production requirements.

SML serves the craft brewing, glass packaging, and high-speed bottling sectors, with equipment used for liquor flasks, beer and wine bottles, pickle jars, and other round or non-round containers. Customers range from growing breweries needing cost-effective automation to high-volume bottling lines requiring heavy-duty, continuous-duty machinery.

