UPDATE companies SET description='SRC Automotive operates from Springfield, Missouri, as an employee-owned manufacturer structured around an Employee Stock Ownership Plan (ESOP). The ownership model ties each worker''s stake to the company''s performance, a design intended to align daily decisions with long-term quality outcomes.

The company remanufactures gasoline, LPG, natural-gas, and marine engines, and also produces newly assembled and industrial engines. Its shop runs 5-axis CNC machining centers, and a dedicated R&D department operates dynamometer test cells for each fuel type. Every unit undergoes complete disassembly, with all components returned to specification using genuine OEM or OEM-validated parts before final testing.

Customers span automotive, marine, and industrial sectors. The remanufactured engines serve as lower-cost service replacements for OEM brands, while the newly assembled and industrial lines address original-equipment and aftermarket demand. The dynamometer capability supports validation across gasoline, LPG, natural-gas, and marine applications.

SRC Automotive positions its process as distinct from repair or rebuild: complete disassembly, specification restoration, OEM-grade parts, and full test cycles backed by warranty. The company also cites its certifications — IATF 16949:2016, ISO 9001:2015, and ISO 14001:2015 — and a circular-economy approach that reduces resource consumption and waste.', certifications=ARRAY['IATF 16949:2016','ISO 9001:2015','ISO 14001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["CNC machining (5-axis)", "Engine remanufacturing", "Engine assembly (newly assembled)", "Industrial engine manufacturing", "Product and manufacturing engineering", "Dynamometer testing (gasoline, LPG, natural gas, marine)", "Complete disassembly and inspection", "OEM parts sourcing and validation", "Product testing and validation"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Marine", "Industrial"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["5-axis CNC machining centers", "Dynamometer test cells (gasoline, LPG, natural gas, marine)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Employee-owned (ESOP) structure aligning workforce incentives with quality", "Remanufacturing process: complete disassembly, parts restored to specification, OEM-validated components", "5-axis CNC machining and in-house dynamometer testing for gasoline, LPG, natural gas, and marine engines", "Certified to IATF 16949:2016, ISO 9001:2015, ISO 14001:2015", "Circular-economy model reducing resource use and waste"], "facts_used": ["Employee-owned (ESOP) company -> /", "Headquarters: Springfield, Missouri -> db", "Certifications: IATF 16949:2016, ISO 9001:2015, ISO 14001:2015 -> /", "CNC machining with 5-axis capability -> /", "Remanufactured engines, newly assembled engines, industrial engines -> /", "R&D department with dynamometer testing for gasoline, LPG, natural gas, marine engines -> /", "Complete disassembly, parts brought back to specification, genuine OEM or OEM validated parts -> /", "Every product thoroughly tested with warranty backing -> /", "Circular economy approach -> /", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "REMANUFACTURED ENGINES NEWLY ASSEMBLED ENGINES INDUSTRIAL ENGINES CNC MACHINING", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/src-automotive/"], "ownership_tags": ["Employee-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='src-automotive-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='SVTronics, Inc. operates from its headquarters in Plano, Texas. While a founding year is not publicly disclosed, the firm has built an advanced electronics manufacturing facility focused on restoring domestic production capacity.

The company provides end-to-end electronics manufacturing services, ranging from prototype to high-volume production. Its capabilities include surface-mount and through-hole PCB assembly, with a dedicated high-speed SMT line and a separate prototype SMT line, automated screen printing with vision inspection, 01005 component placement, wave and selective soldering, conformal coating, mechanical assembly, and wiring and cable harness fabrication. Engineering support covers mechanical and electrical design, new product introduction, system integration, and testing. Order fulfillment and aftermarket services round out the offering.

SVTronics serves military, aerospace, and government customers through its Military Aerospace and Government (MAG) business unit, led by Director Zenon “Bud” Maciekowicz. The company’s quality certifications — including ISO 9001:2015, AS9100D, and ISO 13485 — also position it for medical device and other regulated sectors.

The company emphasizes a “Bring Manufacturing Back to America” mission, highlighting its U.S.-based facility and an online QuickPrice tool that delivers instant quotes with automated DFM/DFA checks and BOM sourcing. ITAR registration further enables work on defense-related programs.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','AS9100D','ISO 13485','ITAR Registered','HUB Certificate','SBE Certificate','IPC 610','IPC 620','SMTA','Minority Business Certification']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["PCB Assembly (SMT and Through-Hole)", "Prototype PCB Assembly", "High-Volume PCB Assembly", "New Product Introduction (NPI)", "Mechanical Engineering Services", "Electrical Engineering Services", "System Integration and Testing", "Cable and Wire Harness Assembly", "Mechanical Assembly", "Conformal Coating", "Automated Screen Printing with Vision Inspection", "01005 Component Placement", "Wave Soldering", "Selective Soldering", "Order Fulfillment and Logistics", "Aftermarket Support Services", "Automated BOM Sourcing", "Online Quoting with DFM/DFA Analysis", "3D Product Rendering", "Gerber and ODB++ File Support"], "industries": ["Military", "Aerospace", "Government"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["High-speed SMT production line", "Prototype SMT production line", "Automated vision screen printers", "Wave soldering equipment", "Selective soldering equipment"], "volume": "Prototype through production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Instant online quoting with automated DFM/DFA analysis and BOM sourcing", "ITAR-registered facility for defense programs", "Minority-owned, HUBZone and Small Business Enterprise certified", "Dedicated high-speed SMT lines for both prototype and volume production", "End-to-end services from engineering through aftermarket support"], "facts_used": ["Company name SVTronics, Inc -> db", "Headquarters Plano, Texas -> db", "Certifications ISO9001, ISO13485, ITAR -> db", "Capabilities list including mechanical/electrical engineering, order fulfillment, 01005 placement, screen printers with vision, conformal coating -> db", "Products list including PCB assembly, cable assemblies, prototype and high-volume production, SMT lines, wave/selective soldering -> db", "Industries served: Military Aerospace & Govt - MAG -> db", "LinkedIn URL -> db", "Homepage: address 3465 Technology Dr Plano, TX 75074, phone, email -> /", "Homepage: certifications ISO 9001:2015, AS9100D, ISO 13485, ITAR Registered, HUB Certificate, SBE Certificate, IPC 610, IPC 620, SMTA, Minority Business Certification -> /", "Homepage: services - New Product Introduction, Electronic Manufacturing, System Integration and Testing, Mechanical and Electrical Engineering, Wiring and Cable Assemblies, Order Fulfillment and Aftermarket Services -> /", "Homepage: online QuickPrice tool with instant quoting, automatic BOM sourcing, DFM/DFA check, Gerber/ODB++ support, 3D rendering -> /", "Homepage: ''Bringing Manufacturing Back to America'' mission, advanced facility in Plano, Texas -> /", "Homepage: fully automated high speed SMT production line, separate SMT line for prototype production -> /", "Homepage: screen printers with automated vision capability, wave and selective soldering, placement capability for 01005 package components -> /", "Homepage: ''We provide all types of manufacturing services for electronics products from prototype thru production'' -> /", "Homepage: Military Aerospace & Govt - MAG business unit, Director Zenon \u201cBud\u201d Maciekowicz -> /"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We provide all types of manufacturing services for electronics products from prototype thru production", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR Registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/svtronics/"], "ownership_tags": ["Minority-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='svtronics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Safe-T-Cap Manufacturing, operating as Auto Rust Technicians, is based in Cranston, Rhode Island, in a 10,000-square-foot facility on the outskirts of Providence. The company was founded in 1977 by Jerry Carlson, an engineer from Detroit, Michigan, who began by welding a friend’s Volkswagen Beetle in his fabrication shop. Over four decades, the team has repaired more than 15,000 vehicles.

The business runs two parallel operations: a service center that restores rusted frames through sandblasting, cutting out corroded sections, and welding in proprietary Safe-T-Cap repair kits; and a manufacturing line that produces those kits. Each kit is built from American-made cold-rolled steel, assembled and welded by certified welders, and designed for installation by qualified technicians worldwide. The product range covers frame sections for Jeep Wrangler, Ford Ranger, F-150, Chevrolet/GMC Silverado and Sierra, Toyota Tacoma, 4Runner, Tundra, and FJ Cruiser, as well as Mopar, Saab, and other models.

The kits are sold internationally via FedEx and USPS, with online sales to the U.S. and Canada.

The Safe-T-Cap line originated as internal tooling for Auto Rust’s own repairs and evolved into a DIY product line to “fix the car without being there.” The company emphasizes domestic materials, over 40 years of research and development, and a specialization it calls “rustorations,” guaranteeing its work while leaving finish bodywork and painting to other specialists.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Vehicle rust repair and restoration", "Sandblasting", "Frame section cutting and fabrication", "Welding (certified welders)", "Manufacturing of frame repair kits", "Cold-rolled steel fabrication", "Kit assembly", "International shipping (FedEx/USPS)", "Installation instruction development"], "industries": ["Automotive aftermarket", "Vehicle restoration", "Off-road/4x4", "Truck/SUV", "Classic car"], "materials": ["Cold-rolled steel (American-made)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Proudly made in the USA using only American-made cold-rolled steel", "Over 40 years of R&D behind Safe-T-Cap frame repair kits", "Each kit assembled and welded by certified welders", "Specialized ''rustoration'' service with guaranteed work", "Kits designed for DIY installation by qualified technicians worldwide"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1977 by Jerry Carlson -> db, /about", "Headquarters in Cranston, Rhode Island -> db, /about", "10,000 sq ft facility -> /about", "Repaired over 15,000 vehicles (home page) / 20,000 vehicles (about page) -> /, /about", "Manufactures Safe-T-Cap frame repair kits from American cold-rolled steel -> /, /about", "Kits for Jeep, Ford, GM, Toyota, Mopar, Saab -> /, /about", "Certified welders assemble kits -> /, /about", "Services: sandblasting, fabrication, preliminary body work -> /about", "International shipping via FedEx/USPS -> /, /about", "No finish body work, paint, mechanical, interior -> /about", "Originated as internal tooling, evolved to DIY kits -> /about", "Guarantees work -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "What was once parts for our own use, has turned into a small manufacturing business.", "founded_year": "1977", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='safe-t-cap-manufacturing' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Safer Textiles was founded in 1975 by Albert Safer in Newark, New Jersey. The privately owned company operates a 180,000-square-foot facility on 5.7 acres in an Urban Enterprise Zone and employs over 125 people.

The mill is vertically integrated, handling knitting, dyeing, finishing, and coating under one roof. Its knitting department produces interlocks, jacquards, jerseys, piques, pontes, and specialty knits from a wide range of yarns. The dye house runs 25-plus modern computer-controlled machines — jets, soft flows, jigs, and atmospheric beams — with lot capacities up to 4,000 pounds and a Datacolor 800 spectrophotometer for color consistency. Finishing includes preparation (desizing, bleaching, scouring), surface treatments (napping, sueding, sanding), and chemical finishes such as flame retardant, moisture management, antimicrobial, and durable water/oil repellent. Coating uses a knife-blade process to apply water-based polyurethane on a 90-foot, 10-zone thermal range.

Safer Textiles serves apparel, medical PPE (masks, gowns meeting Levels 1–3), team sports (antimicrobial, wicking, UV-treated uniforms), military (DOD-spec fabrics), industrial (coated nylon for water/oil repellency), home furnishings, and novelty markets.

The company emphasizes turnaround times, the ability to execute high-volume orders, and a fully stocked warehouse with its own trucking network and global carriers to deliver on time. Its integrated model allows a fabric to move from raw yarn to finished product without leaving the facility, supported by ongoing R&D investment.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Knitting (interlocks, jacquards, jerseys, piques, pontes, specialty knits)", "Dyeing (computerized color matching, disperse/reactive dyes, up to 4,000 lbs/lot)", "Finishing preparation (desizing, bleaching, scouring)", "Finishing surface treatments (napping, sueding, sanding)", "Chemical finishing (flame retardant, moisture management, stain/soil resistant, durable water/oil repellent, antimicrobial, shrinkage control, elastomeric finishing, crease resistant)", "Coating (knife-blade water-based polyurethane, 90-foot 10-zone thermal cure, durable water repellent, flame retardant)", "Quality assurance (Datacolor 800 spectrophotometer, QTX file transfer)"], "industries": ["Apparel", "Medical PPE", "Team Sports", "Military", "Industrial", "Home Furnishings", "Novelty"], "materials": ["100% Polyester / Polyester Blends", "Microdenier", "100% Nylon / Nylon Blends", "Copper", "Silver", "Inherent Antimicrobial yarns", "Spandex Blends", "100% Cotton / Poly Cotton", "Nomex / Nomex Blends", "Recycled Yarns", "Carbon", "Polypropylene", "Inherent Wicking yarns", "Inherent FR yarns", "100% Cotton (up to 18 oz/sq yd)", "100% Polyester and Poly Cotton Blends", "Nylon (Lightweight Ripstop to 1050 Denier Coated Ballistic)"], "equipment": ["25+ modern computer dyeing machines (jets, soft flows, jigs, atmospheric beams)", "Datacolor 800 Spectrophotometer", "90-foot 10-zone thermal range"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vertically integrated mill processing yarn to finished fabric on-site", "Industry-leading turnaround times and high-volume order execution", "25+ computer-controlled dyeing machines with 4,000-lb lot capacity", "Datacolor 800 spectrophotometer for color consistency and QTX file transfer", "90-foot, 10-zone thermal range for coating with knife-blade polyurethane application", "Own trucking network and global carrier partnerships for reliable delivery"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1975 by Albert Safer -> /about-us", "Privately owned by Albert Safer -> /about-us", "180,000 sq. ft. facility on 5.7 acres -> /about-us", "Over 125 employees -> /about-us", "Located in Newark, NJ Urban Enterprise Zone -> /about-us", "Vertically integrated mill (knitting, dyeing, finishing, coating) -> /about-us, /services", "Knitting: interlocks, jacquards, jerseys, piques, pontes, specialty knits -> /services", "Yarns available: polyester, nylon, cotton, spandex, Nomex, recycled, carbon, etc. -> /services", "25+ modern computer dyeing machines (jets, soft flows, jigs, atmospheric beams) -> /services", "Dye lot capacity up to 4,000 pounds -> /services", "Datacolor 800 Spectrophotometer for color consistency -> /services", "Finishing preparation: desizing, bleaching, scouring -> /services", "Surface finishing: napping, sueding, sanding -> /services", "Chemical finishes: flame retardant, moisture management, stain/soil resistant, durable water/oil repellent, antimicrobial, shrinkage control, elastomeric, crease resistant -> /services", "Coating: knife-blade water-based polyurethane, 90-foot 10-zone thermal range -> /services", "Industries served: apparel, medical PPE, team sports, military, industrial, home furnishings, novelty -> /, /about-us", "Medical PPE: masks, uniforms, gowns Levels 1-3 -> /", "Military: DOD standards, successful bids -> /", "Industry-leading turnaround times and high-volume order execution -> /about-us", "Fully stocked warehouse, own trucking network, global carriers -> /about-us", "R&D funding for new product development -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Safer Textiles uses skills and expertise developed over our 50+ year history to turn premium yarns into high quality fabrics", "founded_year": "1975", "employee_count": "125+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='safer-textiles' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Safety Components operates from a 22-acre campus in Greenville, South Carolina, where it has produced technical textiles since 1912. Now a subsidiary of Elevate Textiles, the company traces its roots to over a century of textile expertise in the region.

The 800,000-square-foot facility integrates weaving, coating, finishing, testing, and warehousing under one roof. Skilled associates manufacture a range of industrial fabrics — from flame-resistant outer shells and thermal liners for turnout gear to military-spec technical textiles and WeatherMAX® outdoor and marine fabrics — using substrates such as woven polyesters, nylons, and aramid fibers.

The company supplies the largest fire departments in the United States and worldwide, including the Indianapolis Fire Department, and provides materials to gear manufacturers Lion Apparel, Globe, and Honeywell. Its fabrics also serve military programs, high-performance outdoor brands, and the coating industry.

Safety Components differentiates itself through patented technologies such as Filament Twill Technology™ (2012), which yields lighter, stronger fabrics, and PF Zero™, the first commercially available PFAS-free durable water repellent finish for PPE meeting NFPA 1971. The firm also pursues sustainability targets: 100 percent renewable energy and a 40 percent water-use reduction by 2030.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Technical fabric weaving", "Coating and finishing", "Substrate production (woven polyesters, nylons, aramid)", "Flame-resistant fabric manufacturing", "Thermal liner production", "Military technical textile manufacturing", "Outdoor and marine fabric manufacturing (WeatherMAX\u00ae)", "Research and development", "Testing and quality assurance", "Warehousing and distribution", "Patent development and IP management", "PFAS-free durable water repellent application", "Filament Twill Technology\u2122 implementation"], "industries": ["Fire service / first responders", "Military / defense", "High-performance outdoor", "Marine", "Technical textiles", "Coating industry"], "materials": ["Woven polyesters", "Nylons", "Aramid fibers", "PBI (polybenzimidazole) fibers", "High-performance fibers"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Patented Filament Twill Technology\u2122 (2012) producing lighter, stronger fabrics before and after UV exposure", "First commercially available PFAS-free durable water repellent finish (PF Zero\u2122) for first-responder PPE", "Proprietary PBI Max\u2122 and Glide ICE\u2122 fabrics setting benchmarks for thermal protection and comfort", "800,000 sq ft U.S. facility with integrated manufacturing, testing, and warehousing", "Public sustainability commitments: 100% renewable energy and 40% water reduction by 2030"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1912 -> db, /", "Headquarters Greenville, South Carolina -> db, /about", "22-acre campus, 800,000 sq ft facility -> /about", "Subsid