UPDATE companies SET description='Safety Fresh Foods operates from Glendale, Wisconsin, with a high-pressure processing (HPP) facility in Plymouth, Wisconsin. The company installed a state-of-the-art HPP machine to provide non-thermal pasteurization services to food manufacturers.

The company specializes in high-pressure processing, a cold-water technology that applies up to 87,000 psi to packaged foods for a few seconds to several minutes. The process inactivates pathogens such as Listeria, Salmonella, and E. coli without heat, chemicals, or additives, preserving taste, texture, and nutrients. Shelf life typically increases three to ten times compared to untreated products stored at the same temperature. The equipment also supports cheese ripening control, meat tenderization, and flavor infusion.

Safety Fresh Foods serves food and beverage manufacturers, including dairy, meat, and beverage producers, particularly in Wisconsin. The company works with clients on innovation, cost savings, food safety, shelf-life extension, and process improvements.

