UPDATE companies SET description='Sea Bright Solar was founded in 2003 in Ocean Township, New Jersey. The company began with a focus on helping homeowners and businesses generate renewable energy through solar power, expanding over time to serve customers across New Jersey, New York, and Southern California.

The firm provides turnkey solar and home energy solutions. Its services span solar photovoltaic system design and installation, battery storage (including EcoFlow and SolarEdge systems), EV charging stations, and a Home Upgrade division that handles roofing (GAF-certified), siding (Norandex), gutters, whole-home generators (Generac), and main electrical panel upgrades. The company operates from three locations — Ocean, NJ; Staten Island, NY; and Redlands, CA — and holds active contractor licenses in each jurisdiction.

Sea Bright Solar serves residential and commercial customers seeking energy independence and lower utility costs. Its client base includes homeowners looking to combine solar with roofing or backup power, as well as businesses pursuing sustainability goals. The company also works with customers adding electric vehicles or planning home expansions that increase energy demand.

The company differentiates itself by consolidating multiple trades — roofing, electrical, solar, and generator installation — under a single licensed team, aiming to simplify project management and accountability. It emphasizes the use of high-performance, professional-grade products and over 20 years of combined experience.', certifications=ARRAY['NYC General Contractor License 602644','Westchester County Home Improvement License WC-26292-H13','New Jersey Home Improvement Contractor License 13VH01847600','California CSLB License 900399','Pennsylvania Home Improvement Contractor License PA176800','GAF Certified Roofing Contractor']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar PV system design and installation", "Battery energy storage system installation (EcoFlow, SolarEdge)", "EV charging station installation", "Roofing system installation (GAF-certified)", "Siding installation (Norandex)", "Gutter system installation with critter and snow guards", "Whole-home generator installation (Generac)", "Main electrical panel upgrades", "Smart energy panel installation (SolarEdge hubs, EcoFlow)", "Solar financing and incentive consulting", "Residential and commercial solar consulting", "Home energy efficiency upgrades"], "industries": ["Residential solar", "Commercial solar", "Home improvement and renovation", "Renewable energy installation", "Electrical contracting", "Roofing", "Energy storage", "Backup power generation"], "materials": ["Solar photovoltaic modules", "Lithium-ion battery storage systems (EcoFlow, SolarEdge)", "Asphalt roofing shingles (GAF)", "Vinyl siding (Norandex)", "Natural gas/propane generators (Generac)", "Electrical panel components", "EV charging equipment"], "equipment": ["GAF roofing systems", "Norandex siding", "Generac generators", "EcoFlow battery systems", "SolarEdge hubs and smart energy panels"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Single licensed team manages solar, roofing, electrical, and generator work from consultation to final installation", "Installs professional-grade products: GAF roofing, Norandex siding, Generac generators, EcoFlow and SolarEdge energy systems", "Holds active contractor licenses in New Jersey, New York (NYC and Westchester), California, and Pennsylvania", "Over 20 years of experience designing and installing residential and commercial solar systems", "Offers integrated solar-plus-storage, EV charging, and home upgrade packages"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2003 -> db", "Headquarters Ocean Township, NJ -> db", "Serves NJ, NY, CA -> db", "Home Upgrade division with multiple services -> /about", "Licenses in multiple states -> /about", "Installs GAF roofing, Norandex siding, Generac generators, EcoFlow, SolarEdge -> /about", "Locations in Ocean NJ, Staten Island NY, Redlands CA -> /about", "Team includes consultants, designers, engineers, installation teams -> db", "Offers solar financing and incentives -> db"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Sea Bright Solar''s Home Upgrade division brings together today''s most in-demand services under one roof, making it easier to complete full-scale home solar upgrades. Our licensed team manages every step\u2014from consultation to final installation.", "founded_year": "2003", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sea-bright-solar' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='SeaCa Packaging operates from Dinuba, California, in the heart of the Central Valley. The company was established in 1991 by the owners of Seattle‑Tacoma Box Company, a family business founded in 1889 that had already passed through six generations. SeaCa was created to extend that legacy of reliable service and on‑time delivery to growers and packers in Central California.

The company designs, develops, and manufactures printed corrugated boxes, plastic corrugated (polypropylene) containers, and wooden packaging. It also provides value‑added services such as structural design and graphic printing. The operation serves agricultural, industrial, and seafood customers, though the facility size and headcount are not disclosed.

Primary markets include the fruit, vegetable, and seafood sectors along the West Coast.

SeaCa emphasizes its family heritage, a customer‑focused approach, and a commitment to sustainable packaging solutions. The company says its six‑generation experience allows it to deliver practical, innovative packaging that helps clients stand out in competitive markets.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Printed corrugated packaging manufacturing", "Plastic corrugated (polypropylene) packaging manufacturing", "Wooden packaging manufacturing", "Packaging design and development", "Value-added packaging services (graphic printing, structural design)"], "industries": ["Agricultural", "Industrial", "Seafood", "Fruit and vegetable"], "materials": ["Corrugated cardboard", "Polypropylene corrugated", "Wood"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family legacy spanning six generations", "Commitment to on-time deliveries", "Customer-focused approach", "Sustainable packaging solutions", "Expertise in agricultural and seafood packaging"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1991 by six-generation packaging company -> /", "Headquarters in Dinuba, California -> db", "Manufactures printed corrugated, plastic corrugated, and wooden packaging -> /", "Serves agricultural, industrial, seafood markets -> /", "Family legacy, reliable service, customer-focused approach -> /", "Sustainability focus -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We design, develop, and manufacture a variety of products for the agricultural, industrial, and seafood markets.", "founded_year": "1991", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='seaca-packaging' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The business traces its roots through six generations of the founding family, who have maintained ownership and operational control since the late 19th century. In 1991 the family expanded its footprint by launching SeaCa Packaging to serve Central California with graphic packaging, and in 2014 added SeaCa Plastic Packaging for sustainable polypropylene corrugated products. A sister operation, Commencement Bay Corrugated, was established in the early 1980s as an independent corrugated plant jointly owned by the presidents of Seattle-Tacoma Box Company and Pacific Container Company.

The company manufactures a full range of corrugated, plastic, and wooden packaging at dedicated wood and corrugated plants.

