UPDATE companies SET description='Secure Semiconductor Manufacturing, LLC (SSM) operates from Lebo, Kansas, as a 100% American-owned and operated advanced electronics manufacturer. The company was founded with a mission to restore critical electronics manufacturing capabilities to the United States by providing secure, reliable, and high-quality PCB fabrication and assembly services for commercial, industrial, aerospace, defense, medical, energy, telecommunications, and critical infrastructure markets.

SSM provides printed circuit board (PCB) fabrication, printed circuit board assembly (PCBA), surface mount technology (SMT) assembly, through-hole assembly, and mixed-technology assembly including RF. The facility supports prototype through low-to-medium volume production with quick-turn manufacturing, design for manufacturability (DFM) support, automated optical inspection (AOI), quality inspection and testing, conformal coating, potting, high-density interconnect (HDI) and controlled impedance capabilities, counterfeit component prevention, and traceability. Workmanship meets IPC-A-610 Class 3 standards.

The company serves aerospace and avionics, defense and government contracting, medical devices and health technology, energy and industrial automation, telecommunications and wireless infrastructure, as well as commercial and industrial innovators. SSM also supports startups and commercial product developers with scalable, cost-effective PCB solutions, full engineering support, BOM optimization, component sourcing, and rapid domestic prototyping.

SSM differentiates itself through 100% U.S.-based manufacturing, ITAR registration, AS9100 and ISO 9001 certified processes, full confidentiality and traceability, and responsive engineering support. Its stated mission extends beyond manufacturing to eliminating reliance on offshore electronics production, enhancing national security and supply chain resiliency, fostering domestic economic growth, and delivering environmentally responsible manufacturing.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','AS9100','ITAR']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Printed Circuit Board (PCB) Fabrication", "Printed Circuit Board Assembly (PCBA)", "Surface Mount Technology (SMT) Assembly", "Through-Hole Assembly", "Mixed-technology assembly (SMT, through-hole, RF)", "Prototype and Low-to-Medium Volume Production", "Quick-Turn Manufacturing", "Design for Manufacturability (DFM) Support", "Automated Optical Inspection (AOI)", "Quality Inspection and Testing", "Supply Chain and Manufacturing Support", "Conformal Coating", "Potting", "High-Density Interconnect (HDI)", "Controlled Impedance PCB Capabilities", "Counterfeit Component Prevention", "Traceability", "IPC-A-610 Class 3 Workmanship", "Engineer-Supported Service", "Bare Board Production", "Component Manufacturing"], "industries": ["Aerospace & Avionics", "Defense & Government Contracting", "Medical Devices & Health Technology", "Energy & Industrial Automation", "Telecommunications & Wireless Infrastructure", "Commercial", "Industrial", "Critical Infrastructure"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype to low-to-medium volume production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["100% U.S.-based manufacturing", "ITAR-registered with AS9100 and ISO 9001 certified processes", "Full confidentiality and traceability", "Responsive engineering and technical support", "Proven track record across defense, aerospace, and commercial sectors"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Lebo, Kansas -> db", "100% American-owned and operated -> /about", "Founded to restore U.S. electronics manufacturing -> /about", "PCB fabrication, PCBA, SMT, through-hole, mixed-technology assembly -> /about", "Prototype to low-to-medium volume, quick-turn, DFM, AOI, inspection, conformal coating, potting, HDI, controlled impedance, counterfeit prevention, traceability -> /about", "IPC-A-610 Class 3 workmanship -> /about, db", "Industries: aerospace, defense, medical, energy, telecom, commercial, industrial, critical infrastructure -> /about", "Startup/commercial support with engineering, BOM optimization, sourcing -> /about", "ITAR registered, AS9100, ISO 9001 certified -> /about, db", "Mission: eliminate offshore reliance, enhance national security, domestic growth, environmentally responsible -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Secure Semiconductor Manufacturing (SSM) is a 100% American-owned and operated advanced electronics manufacturing company dedicated to strengthening the United States supply chain through domestic printed circuit board (PCB) fabrication and printed circuit board assembly (PCBA).", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='secure-semiconductor-manufacturing-llc-office' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='The company maintains its corporate headquarters in Reno and operates a sales network of direct representatives and authorized distributors across North America and Mexico.

Selco designs and manufactures a broad line of temperature controls, including disc thermostats, remote capillary controls, probe thermostats, NTC thermistors with interchangeable accuracies of ±0.05°C to ±1.0°C, electronic temperature controls, thermal protectors, digital panel meters, and custom wire harness assemblies. Manufacturing capabilities span mechanical engineering, probe design, PCB layout (AutoCAD, SolidWorks), SMT pick-and-place (Juki), convection reflow (Lovell), wave soldering, epoxy potting, and wire cutting, stripping, and crimping. Production runs from prototypes to full volume, supported by a Reno facility and exclusive manufacturing partnerships in Brazil, China, Italy, Mexico, Japan, and Taiwan.

The company serves HVAC, medical, electronics, professional audio, industrial instrumentation, power supply, food service, appliances, process controls, telecommunications, aerospace, and laboratory markets. Customers include foodservice equipment makers such as Proluxe and AJ Antunes, ice machine manufacturer Ice-O-Matic, compressor supplier VMAC, and a German freezestat producer that transitioned four models to Selco. Distributors handle small-quantity and repair orders.

Selco’s stated mission is to manufacture and supply quality, innovative thermal management products with outstanding worldwide service. Differentiators cited include an ISO 9001:2015 quality system, just-in-time and Kanban inventory programs, same-day shipping from Reno for stocked parts, engineering support with thermal testing and failure analysis, a one-year warranty, and free samples in most cases.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2008','ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Mechanical Engineering", "Probe Design", "Custom Brackets", "Wire Harness Assembly", "AutoCAD", "SolidWorks", "PCB Design", "Cable Fixture Design", "Test Fixture Design", "Thermal Testing", "Failure Analysis", "Troubleshooting", "Design Review", "Solder Screen Printing", "SMT Pick and Place (Juki)", "Convection Reflow Oven (Lovell)", "Wave Soldering", "PCB Assembly and Rework", "Epoxy Potting", "Cable and Wire Cutting and Stripping", "Wire Crimping", "Custom Temperature Control Manufacturing", "Thermistor Manufacturing", "Thermal Protector Manufacturing"], "industries": ["HVAC", "Medical", "Electronics", "Professional audio", "Industrial instrumentation", "Power Supply", "Food Service", "Appliances", "Process Controls", "Telecommunications", "Aerospace", "Laboratory"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Juki SMT Pick and Place", "Lovell Convection Reflow Oven", "Wave Solder", "PCB Assembly and Rework Stations", "Solder Screen", "Cable and Wire Cutting and Stripping machines", "Wire Crimping machines"], "volume": "Prototypes to volume production", "lead_time": "Same-day shipping for stocked items from Reno, Nevada", "tolerances": "\u00b10.05\u00b0C to \u00b11.0\u00b0C for NTC thermistors", "built_on": ["Same-day shipping from Reno, Nevada for stocked parts", "ISO 9001:2015 certified quality system", "Just-in-time and Kanban inventory programs", "Engineering support including thermal testing and failure analysis", "Free samples in most cases"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1958 -> db", "Headquarters Reno, Nevada -> db", "ISO 9001:2008 certification -> /", "ISO 9001:2015 certification -> /about-us", "Manufacturing facilities in Reno, Nevada and partnerships in Brazil, China, Italy, Mexico, Japan, Taiwan -> /about-us", "Product lines: disc thermostats, remote capillary controls, probe thermostats, NTC thermistors, electronic temperature controls, thermal protectors, digital panel meters, custom wire harness assemblies -> / and /about-us", "Industries served: HVAC, Medical, Electronics, Professional audio, Industrial instrumentation, Power Supply, Food Service, Appliances, Process Controls, Telecommunications, Aerospace, Laboratory -> /about-us", "Engineering capabilities: Mechanical Engineering, Probe Design, Custom Brackets, Wire Harness, AutoCAD, SolidWorks, PCB Design, Cable Fixture Design, Test Fixture Design, Thermal testing, Failure Analysis, Troubleshooting, Design Review -> /about-us", "Manufacturing capabilities: Solder Screen, Juki SMT Pick and Place, Lovell Convection Reflow Oven, Wave Solder, PCB Assembly and Rework Stations, Epoxy Potting, Cable and Wire Cutting and Stripping, Wire Crimping -> /about-us", "Strengths: Same day shipping from Reno, Nevada; JIT program; Kanban program; One-year warranty; Engineering support; Free samples -> /about-us", "Volume range: Prototypes to volume production -> /about-us", "Tolerances: NTC thermistor interchangeable accuracies \u00b10.05\u00b0C to \u00b11.0\u00b0C -> /", "Family-owned implication from customer testimonial -> /", "Customer examples: Proluxe, VMAC, Ice-O-Matic, AJ Antunes, German freezestat manufacturer -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Selco Products distributes and manufactures temperature controls.", "founded_year": "1958", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='selco-products-company' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Selvaggio Steel, Inc. operates from Springfield, Illinois, where it was founded in 1957 by Joe Selvaggio after he returned from World War II. Joe, supported by his wife Helen and his brother Jasper, started the business as Selvaggio Ornamental & Structural Steel Inc., building a reputation for custom ornamental ironwork. The company remains family-owned, now led by the second generation—sons Mark and Tony, who began as teenagers on the shop floor, and daughter Michelle, who joined as comptroller.

The shop provides structural steel fabrication and ornamental ironwork, handling drilling, punching, welding, shearing, torch burning, brake pressing, and plate rolling. Its 30-person crew runs a highly automated facility equipped with a CNC beam drill line with robotic coping, CNC angle fabricator, CNC plate punch with plasma cutting, CNC profile and plate rolls, and a 400-ton brake press. Detailing is done in-house using the SDS/2 3D CAD system, and the shop also offers sandblasting, special coatings, field installation, and crane rental with a 110-foot boom.

Customers include healthcare projects such as the Koke Mill Medical Center and Memorial Medical Center’s emergency department and pedestrian walkway, along with commercial and residential builders needing structural steel, stairs, rails, columns, trellises, and custom metalwork. The company’s warehouse supplies raw steel—plate, pipe, tubing, stainless, decking, and structural shapes—in quantities from a single piece to full truckloads.

Selvaggio Steel distinguishes itself through early technology adoption: it was the first Illinois fabricator to use 3D CAD for steel and secured AISC certification in 2007, regarded as the industry’s gold standard. Millions invested in automation have consolidated multiple operations into single-button processes, reducing labor and lead times. The family’s guiding principle—treating others as they wish to be treated—underpins long-standing client and supplier relationships.', certifications=ARRAY['AISC Certification (American Institute of Steel Construction)','AWS Certified Welder']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Structural steel fabrication", "Ornamental iron fabrication", "3D CAD steel detailing (SDS/2)", "CNC beam drilling with robotic coping", "CNC angle fabricating", "CNC plate punching with plasma cutting", "CNC profile rolling", "CNC plate rolling", "400-ton brake pressing", "AWS-certified welding", "Sandblasting and special coatings", "Field installation", "Crane rental (110-foot boom)", "Steel warehouse supply (cut-to-length)"], "industries": ["Healthcare construction", "Commercial construction", "Residential construction", "Industrial construction"], "materials": ["Steel plate", "Pipe and tubing", "Stainless steel", "Roof and floor decks", "Angle", "Flat", "Channel", "House beams and posts", "Bumper posts"], "equipment": ["CNC beam drill line with saw & robotic coping", "CNC angle fabricating machine", "CNC plate punch with plasma cutting machine", "CNC profile roll", "CNC plate roll", "400-ton brake press", "SDS/2 computer detailing system", "110-foot boom crane"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["First Illinois fabricator to adopt 3D CAD (SDS/2) for steel detailing", "AISC certified since 2007, recognized as the industry\u2019s gold standard for fabricators", "Heavily automated shop with CNC beam drill line, robotic coping, plasma cutting, and 400-ton brake press", "Union workforce with AWS-certified welders", "Warehouse stocks raw steel available by the piece or truckload"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1957 by Joe Selvaggio -> /about-us", "Family-owned, second-generation management -> /about-us", "30 employees -> /about-us", "AISC Certified since 2007 -> /about-us and /services", "AWS Certified Welders -> / and /services", "First in Illinois to use 3D CAD (SDS/2) for steel -> /about-us", "Automated facility with CNC beam drill line, CNC angle fabricator, CNC plate punch with plasma, CNC profile/plate rolls, 400-ton brake press -> /services", "Union steel fabrication personnel -> / and /services", "Projects: Koke Mill Medical Center, Memorial Medical Center Emergency, Memorial Medical Center Pedestrian Walkway -> /about-us", "Warehouse supplies raw steel from single piece to truckload -> /services", "Crane rental with 110-foot boom, low minimums -> /services", "Field installation offered -> /services", "Ornamental iron: custom design, stairs, rails, columns, trellises, fire pits -> /services", "Materials: steel plate, pipe, tubing, stainless, decking, structural shapes -> /services", "Headquarters: Springfield, Illinois -> / and db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "From structural steel fabrication to ornamental iron work, Selvaggio Steel is known for its technical precision and leadership in the industry.", "founded_year": "1957", "employee_count": "30", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='selvaggio-steel-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='SemiGen, Inc. was founded in 2009 in Londonderry, New Hampshire, to serve as a multi‑faceted partner for electronic device manufacturers. The company operates a 43,000‑square‑foot facility with 20,000 square feet of clean‑room space, housing RF/microwave assembly, automated PCB assembly, and testing under one roof. Now a subsidiary of Naprotek (an Edgewater Capital Partners portfolio company), SemiGen acts as an on‑demand extension of customers’ engineering and production teams.

SemiGen manufactures its own semiconductor and passive components — PIN, Schottky, and step‑recovery diodes, thin‑film circuits, filters, and attenuators — while also providing contract manufacturing: thermo‑compression and ultrasonic wire bonding, ball bonding, fine‑pitch and BGA PCB assembly, and box‑build. Its in‑house ion‑beam foundry offers thin‑film processing, metallization, wafer dicing, and ion‑beam milling. A test lab supports RF/microwave performance testing and high‑reliability MIL‑STD screening up to 50 GHz. Over $3 million in recent equipment investments supports capacity.

The company serves military electronics, commercial products, and medical instrumentation markets, with compliance to space‑level MIL‑PRF‑38534 and military MIL‑PRF‑19500, 750, and 883 specs. SemiGen holds CMMC 2.0 Level 2 certification for defense cybersecurity and earned a BAE Systems Partner 2 Win Silver Tier Award.

SemiGen combines product supply — via its RF Supply Store stocking bonding tools and materials — with manufacturing, testing, and foundry services. Its quality system is ISO 9001:2015 certified and built around military‑spec compliance. The firm emphasizes workforce training, cross‑training, and lessons‑learned reviews to reduce risk on repeat jobs, positioning itself as a supply‑chain link for time‑critical, high‑frequency programs.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','CMMC 2.0 Level 2']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["RF/Microwave Assembly", "Automated PCB Assembly", "Thermo-compression Wire Bonding", "Ultrasonic Wire Bonding", "Ball Bonding", "Fine-pitch PCB Assembly", "BGA/QFP PCB Assembly", "Box Build Assembly", "RF/Microwave Performance Testing (up to 50 GHz)", "High-reliability / MIL-STD Screening", "Thin Film Processing", "Metallization", "Wafer Dicing", "Ion Beam Milling", "Foundry Services (Ion Beam)", "Electrical, Mechanical, Environmental Testing", "Design, Repair and Supply Solutions", "RF Supply Store (Bonding Tools & Materials Distribution)"], "industries": ["Military Electronics", "Commercial Products", "Medical Instrumentation", "Defense / Aerospace", "RF/Microwave Markets", "Space (MIL-PRF-38534)"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Ion Beam Foundry Equipment", "High-Frequency Design, Assembly and Test Equipment", "Automated PCB Assembly Equipment", "RF/Microwave Test Lab Equipment (up to 50 GHz)"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["43,000 sq ft facility with 20,000 sq ft clean room", "Over $3M invested in new equipment and automation", "ISO 9001:2015 quality system with military spec compliance (MIL-PRF 38534, 19500, 750, 883)", "CMMC 2.0 Level 2 certification for defense cybersecurity", "In-house ion beam foundry for thin film circuits"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2009 -> /about", "Headquarters Londonderry, NH -> /about", "43,000 sq ft facility with 20,000 sq ft clean room -> /about", "ISO 9001:2015 certification -> /about", "Military specs MIL-PRF 38534, 19500, 750, 883 -> /about", "Over $3M in new equipment and automation -> /about", "RF/microwave assembly, automated PCB assembly, testing up to 50 GHz -> /services", "Thin film processing, metallization, wafer dicing, ion beam milling -> /services", "Industries: military electronics, commercial products, medical instrumentation -> /services", "CMMC 2.0 Level 2 certification -> /", "BAE Systems Partner 2 Win Silver Tier Award -> /", "Acquisition by Naprotek (Edgewater Capital Partners) -> /about", "Products: PIN, Schottky, step recovery diodes, thin film circuits, filters, attenuators, bonding tools -> /about", "RF Supply Store -> /", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "SemiGen is a full service microwave solutions company that provides advanced microwave assembly, products and services", "founded_year": "2009", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/semigen-inc./"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='semigen-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Sensor Electronics Corporation, headquartered in Savage, Minnesota, was founded in 1991. The company has focused exclusively on industrial gas detection since its inception.

The company designs and manufactures rugged, reliable industrial gas detectors and gas analyzers, including process gas analyzer parts, sterilization analyzer parts, and explosion-proof sensor separation kits. Its product line covers detection of over 100 toxic and combustible gases, ranging from common hazards like methane and carbon monoxide to exotic substances such as titanium tetrachloride. Sensor Electronics also develops custom detection solutions for gases not in its standard catalog.

Sensor Electronics serves industries that require continuous monitoring of hazardous gases, with a noted focus on biogas and renewable energy applications.

