UPDATE companies SET description='Service Steel, Inc. is based in Huntsville, Alabama, and has operated as a family-owned steel fabricator since its founding in 1965. Herb Taylor established the company and led it for 40 years until his passing in 2008; his sons Monty and Matt Taylor now continue the business. Over the decades the firm expanded from a modest shop to a 49,750-square-foot operating area that includes a 13,500-square-foot structural steel fabrication facility, with 243 solar panels supplying most of its energy needs.

The company provides end-to-end structural steel services: estimating, design detailing and engineering using 3D modeling and CAD, CNC drilling, and a full range of fabrication processes including shearing, cambering, sawing, plasma cutting, shot blasting, oxy-fuel cutting, precision leveling, slitting, blanking, hot-dip galvanizing, coating, and end finishing. The shop runs overhead crane systems and a CNC drill line, and the 27-person team also handles erection on site. In addition to custom fabrication, Service Steel stocks angles, channels, beams, pipe, tubing, sheet, plate, expanded metal, flat bar, round and square stock, bar joist, decking, and rebar for immediate sale.

Customers span commercial, industrial, retail, education, healthcare, multi-family, government, power generation, distribution, sports, hospitality, convention, and bridge projects. General contractors, construction managers, developers, and individual buyers have relied on the firm for structures such as office buildings, parking decks, schools, college campuses, aviation facilities, government buildings, power plants, distribution centers, sports arenas, hotels, convention centers, and pedestrian bridges. Notable projects include work at Rikers Island Prison in New York City and jobs in Oklahoma.

Service Steel emphasizes its family-owned culture, AISC certification for conventional and complex building structures, and a one-stop-shop model that combines engineering, fabrication, erection, and material supply under one roof. The company states that its approachable team and willingness to handle orders of any size set it apart.', certifications=ARRAY['AISC Certified (Conventional Steel Structures and Complex Building Structures)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Structural steel fabrication", "Structural steel erection", "Estimating", "Design detailing and engineering", "3D modeling", "CAD", "CNC drilling", "Shearing", "Structural cambering", "Sawing", "Plasma cutting", "Shot blasting", "Oxy-fuel cutting", "Precision leveling", "Slitting", "Blanking", "Hot dip galvanizing", "Coating", "End finishing", "Steel stock sales"], "industries": ["Commercial", "Industrial", "Retail", "Education", "Healthcare", "Multi-family", "Government", "Power generation", "Distribution", "Sports", "Hospitality", "Convention", "Bridge construction", "Office buildings", "Parking decks", "Schools", "College campuses", "Aviation facilities"], "materials": ["Structural steel (carbon steel)", "Angles", "Channels", "Beams", "Pipe", "Tubing", "Sheet", "Plate", "Expanded metal", "Flat bar", "Round stock", "Square stock", "Bar joist", "Decking", "Rebar"], "equipment": ["CNC drill line system", "Overhead crane systems", "3D modeling and CAD systems"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned and operated since 1965", "AISC certified for conventional and complex building structures", "49,750 sq ft facility with 243 solar panels providing most energy", "Comprehensive in-house estimating, detailing, fabrication, and erection", "One-stop shopping for structural steel stock and custom fabrication"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1965 -> db", "Family-owned and operated -> /about-us", "Herb Taylor founder, Monty & Matt Taylor continue -> /about-us", "Facility: 13,5