UPDATE companies SET description='Service Wire Co was founded in 1968 in Culloden, West Virginia, as a family-owned wire and cable manufacturer. The company remains multi-generation family-owned and operates its corporate headquarters in Culloden, with additional offices in Houston, Texas, and Phoenix, Arizona.

The company produces a range of wire and cable products including bare copper, single conductors, twisted cables, tray cable, armored cables, VFD cable systems, and submersible pump cable. Manufacturing is supported by an in-house UL laboratory that tests every order, and an ISO 9001:2015 certified quality management system. The firm emphasizes same-day shipping from stock for one- to two-day delivery and offers 24/7 emergency service year-round.

Service Wire serves heavy commercial, industrial, utility, renewable energy, and pump markets across North America, with a dedicated Canadian division. Its products are specified for applications such as EV charging infrastructure, roadway lighting, semiconductor manufacturing, and overhead power distribution.

The company differentiates itself by sourcing and manufacturing 100% of its copper wire and cable in the United States, holding BABA compliance and NEMA''s Make It American Certification. A recent groundbreaking in Culloden signals a major manufacturing expansion to support growing demand.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','BABA Certified','NEMA Certification','Make It American Certification']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wire and cable manufacturing", "Bare copper manufacturing", "Single conductor manufacturing", "Twisted cable assembly", "Tray cable manufacturing", "Armored cable manufacturing", "VFD cable system manufacturing", "Pump cable manufacturing", "Emergency service (24/7)", "Cable management", "Inventory management", "Packaging and pulling", "Reel return", "Quality systems", "In-house UL lab testing", "Certified test reports", "Same-day shipping", "BABA compliance certification"], "industries": ["Heavy Commercial", "Industrial", "Utility", "Renewable Energy", "Pump", "Canada"], "materials": ["Copper", "Aluminum", "XLPE (Cross-linked Polyethylene)", "PVC", "LSZH (Low Smoke Zero Halogen)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Same-day shipping for stocked items, 1-2 day delivery; 24/7 emergency service", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["100% U.S.-sourced and manufactured copper wire and cable", "BABA compliant and NEMA Make It American certified", "24/7 emergency service, 365 days a year", "Same-day shipping on stocked items for 1\u20132 day delivery", "ISO 9001:2015 certified quality system with in-house UL lab testing"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1968 -> db", "Headquarters Culloden, WV -> db", "Family-owned -> /", "Manufactures wire and cable -> /", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /quality", "In-house UL lab -> /quality", "24/7 emergency service -> /", "Same-day shipping -> /quality", "BABA certified -> /", "Make It American Certification -> /", "Markets served: Heavy Commercial, Industrial, Utility, Renewable Energy, Pump, Canada -> /", "Brands: ServicePLEX, ServiceDRIVE, ServicePRO-X, RAINBOW WIRE, ServiceGUARD, EnviroPLUS -> /", "100% U.S. sourced and manufactured -> /", "Expansion in Culloden -> /", "Locations: Houston TX, Phoenix AZ -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Service Wire is a multi-generation, family-owned wire and cable manufacturer and has been since 1968.", "founded_year": "1968", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/service-wire-company_2/"], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='service-wire-co' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Sewer Cable Equipment Co. was founded in 1959 by Don Catterall and Jack Bollinger in Sunland, California. Don, a plumber by trade, invented the Burton Powersnake, a rugged sewer cable machine that became an industry standard. The company relocated to Las Vegas in 1990 and remained family-owned; after Don''s passing in 2013, his daughter Kristie Catterall Allen and grandson Kirk assumed daily operations. In 2024 the business was acquired by Hotsy of Las Vegas and now operates from Henderson, Nevada.

The company manufactures American-made sewer cables in-house and provides expert repair services for sewer cable machines, jetters, cameras, and cables across all major brands. It also stocks and sells equipment and parts from Ridgid, Spartan Tool, General Pipe Cleaners, Gorlitz, and Warthog as an authorized dealer. Technicians handle drum service, motor and transmission work, and feed assembly troubleshooting, offering both OEM and aftermarket replacement parts.

Sewer Cable Equipment serves plumbing and drain-cleaning professionals throughout the Las Vegas region and as far as St. George, Utah.

The business was built on the principle of "reliability, trust, and consistency" — values articulated in early company literature as "timeless principles that express stability and strength during times of rapid growth and change." Founded by plumbers for plumbers, it continues to prioritize dependable equipment and responsive support for the trades that keep infrastructure flowing.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Sewer cable manufacturing", "Sewer equipment repair (cable machines, jetters, cameras, cables)", "Sewer equipment sales (authorized dealer for Ridgid, Spartan, General Pipe Cleaners, Gorlitz, Warthog)", "Spartan Tool repair (machines, snakes, camera systems)", "Sewer camera repair", "Drum service and cleaning", "Motor and transmission service", "Feed assembly troubleshooting", "Replacement parts and service kits (OEM and aftermarket)", "Spartan-compatible sewer cable manufacturing", "General Pipe Cleaners repair services"], "industries": ["Plumbing", "Drain cleaning"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Burton Powersnake", "Gen-Eye POD", "Spartan Tool", "Ridgid", "General Pipe Cleaners", "Gorlitz", "Warthog"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["American-made sewer cables manufactured in-house", "Technicians trained across all major sewer equipment brands", "Authorized Spartan Tool dealer and repair center", "Family-owned legacy since 1959, now backed by Hotsy of Las Vegas", "Local service in Las Vegas with coverage to St. George, Utah"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1959 in Sunland, California by Don Catterall and Jack Bollinger -> /about-us", "Relocated to Las Vegas in 1990 -> /about-us", "Family-owned; daughter and grandson took over after 2013 -> /about-us", "Acquired by Hotsy of Las Vegas in 2024 -> /about-us", "Manufactures American-made sewer cables in-house -> /", "Repairs sewer cable machines, jetters, cameras, and cables -> /", "Authorized dealer for Ridgid, Spartan, General Pipe Cleaners, Gorlitz, Warthog -> /", "Services Spartan Tool equipment as authorized repair center -> /", "Headquarters in Henderson, Nevada -> db", "Founded year 1959 -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We repair sewer equipment, sell parts, and manufacture high-quality sewer cables", "founded_year": "1959", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sewer-cable-equipment-co' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Shaker Style Handcrafted Furniture was founded in 1989 by Stephen C. Barlow in Harrisville, New Hampshire. A third-generation New England woodworker, Barlow began the business to continue a family tradition of craftsmanship passed down from his grandfather and great-grandfather. In 1997 his wife Cheryl joined the operation, bringing sales and design experience to what remains a small, family-run workshop. The company is a member of the League of New Hampshire Craftsmen.

The workshop produces a line of Shaker-inspired furniture including beds, chests, dressers, dining chairs, dining tables, accent tables, and office pieces. Each item is handcrafted from North American hardwoods — primarily New England maple, black cherry from the Allegheny Plateau, and walnut from Missouri riverbanks — using traditional joinery such as dovetails and pegged mortise-and-tenon. Finishes are applied in a three-step process: fine sanding, multiple coats of hand-rubbed oil, and a final hand-waxed, buffed surface.

Barlow has stated that the business was founded on the principle that furniture should last for generations, not end up in a landfill.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Handcrafted furniture manufacturing", "Traditional joinery (dovetail, pegged mortise and tenon)", "Hand-rubbed oil finishing", "Hand waxing and buffing", "Custom furniture design", "White-glove blanket-wrapped delivery", "Sustainable hardwood sourcing"], "industries": [], "materials": ["North American hardwoods", "New England maple", "Black cherry", "Walnut"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Handcrafted using traditional dovetail and pegged mortise-and-tenon joinery", "Three-step hand-rubbed oil and wax finish for durability and repairability", "North American hardwoods sourced from sustainably managed forests", "Direct-from-maker sales with optional white-glove delivery", "Member of the League of New Hampshire Craftsmen"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1989 by Stephen C. Barlow -> db", "Headquarters Harrisville, New Hampshire -> db", "Stephen C. Barlow is a third-generation New England woodworker -> /about", "Cheryl Barlow joined in 1997 -> /about", "Member of the League of New Hampshire Craftsmen -> /about", "Produces beds, chests, dressers, dining chairs, dining tables, accent tables, office furniture -> /", "Handcrafted with North American hardwoods including maple, cherry, walnut -> /", "Uses traditional joinery: dovetails, pegged mortise and tenon -> /about", "Three-step hand-rubbed oil and wax finish -> /about", "Offers white-glove blanket-wrapped delivery -> /about", "Sells directly to customers -> /about", "Committed to sustainability, sourcing hardwoods from renewable forests -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "We are the makers of your fine furniture.", "founded_year": "1989", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "