UPDATE companies SET description='Shamrock Foodservice Warehouse, founded in 1926, opened its Phoenix, Arizona location in January 2015 as a 30,000-square-foot retail warehouse at 2430 W. Indian School Road. The company operates as a wholesale restaurant supply store open to the public with no membership required.

The Phoenix facility stocks more than 7,000 items (with the store manager citing 15,000+), ranging from fresh meats, seafood, produce, and dairy to disposables, kitchen supplies, dry goods, and grocery products. The assortment includes hundreds of Arizona-grown or manufactured items and a selection tailored to the Hispanic market. Services include buy-online-pick-up-in-store and phone orders with products ready for pickup.

The store serves food trucks, caterers, small businesses, and the general public, positioning itself as a one-stop shop for foodservice operators in the Phoenix area. It is open seven days a week from 7 a.m. to 7 p.m.

… We treat our customers like friends!” The company also promotes a “Think local. Shop Shamrock.” approach, highlighting Arizona brands.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Foodservice distribution", "Wholesale restaurant supply", "Retail warehouse operations", "Online ordering with in-store pickup", "Phone order fulfillment", "Local product sourcing"], "industries": ["Foodservice", "Restaurant", "Catering", "Food truck", "Small business", "Retail (public)"], "materials": ["Meats", "Seafood", "Produce", "Dairy", "Disposables", "Kitchen supplies", "Dry goods", "Grocery products", "Hispanic market ingredients"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["30,000-square-foot retail warehouse in Phoenix", "7,000+ stocked items (manager cites 15,000+)", "No membership required, open to the public", "Buy online, pick up in-store; phone orders ready for pickup", "Hundreds of Arizona-grown or manufactured products"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1926 -> db", "Headquarters in Phoenix, Arizona -> db", "Phoenix location opened January 2015 -> /", "30,000-square-foot retail warehouse -> /", "Open to public, no membership required -> /", "Carries 7,000+ items (manager cites 15,000+) -> /", "Product categories: meats, seafood, produce, dairy, disposables, kitchen supplies, dry goods, grocery products, Hispanic market items -> /", "Hundreds of Arizona-grown or manufactured items -> /", "Services: buy online pick up in-store, phone orders ready for pickup -> /", "Serves food trucks, caterers, small businesses, general public -> /", "Hours: Monday-Sunday 7am-7pm -> /", "Manager quote about one-stop shop, personal service, treat customers like friends -> /", "Think local, Shop Shamrock, carries local brands -> /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Shamrock Foodservice Warehouse opened its Phoenix location in January 2015 as a one-stop solution for food & restaurant supply assisting: food trucks, caterers, small businesses, and more.", "founded_year": "1926", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='shamrock-foodservice-warehouse' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Shamrock Plastics was founded in 1989 by Tom Ruffner in Mount Vernon, Ohio. The family-owned business began in a modest 10-by-20-foot storage space, with Ruffner drumming up work by going door to door after learning the trade out of high school and attending ITT Technical College. In 2012, Ruffner and his wife Deb relocated to Myrtle Beach, South Carolina, leaving the Ohio operation in the hands of their son Jay.

The company specializes in custom plastic fabrication, offering services from design and cutting through production and distribution. With facilities in both Mount Vernon and Myrtle Beach, the team draws on more than 100 years of combined experience in plastic fabrication. Shamrock handles domestic and international shipping for finished parts, managing the entire process from initial concept to delivery.

Shamrock serves customers across a range of industries that require custom plastic components, though specific sectors are not detailed in its public materials. The company emphasizes a client-focused approach, treating each project with the same care regardless of size or complexity.

The founders built the business on a philosophy of not cutting corners, promising consistent quality, on-time delivery, and on-budget performance. That family-oriented culture, combined with deep technical expertise, is presented as the core differentiator.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom plastic fabrication", "Design assistance", "Cutting and machining", "Production", "Distribution", "Domestic shipping", "International shipping"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Family-owned business treating clients like family", "Over 100 years of combined team experience in plastic fabrication", "Two facilities in Mount Vernon, OH and Myrtle Beach, SC", "Domestic and international shipping managed in-house", "Commitment to on-time, on-budget delivery"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1989 in Mount Vernon, Ohio by Tom Ruffner -> /", "Family-owned business -> db description", "Started in 10x20 storage space, door-to-door sales -> /", "Second location opened in Myrtle Beach, SC in 2012 -> /", "Ohio location managed by son Jay Ruffner -> /", "More than 100 years combined team experience -> /", "Services: custom plastic fabrication, design, cutting, production, distribution -> /", "Domestic and international shipping handled -> db products", "Commitment to on-time, on-budget delivery -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "custom plastic fabrication company", "founded_year": "1989", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='shamrock-plastics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Shawmut Infinite operates from Burlington, North Carolina, as a subsidiary of Shawmut Corporation. The facility carries a legacy of over 50 years as a textile supplier, formerly known as Fairystone Fabrics before its rebranding to Shawmut Infinite in 2024.

The company specializes in warp knitting, tricot warping, and suedeing, with a focus on automotive interior and industrial fabrics. It runs a large array of Karl Mayer warp knitting machines capable of 168–210-inch widths and 24- to 36-gauge, 2- to 4-bar tricot constructions. Four tricot warpers handle fine denier filament yarns (15/1 to 300 denier) including nylon, polyester, textured and flat yarns, low-melt polyester, and polypropylene. A multi-million-dollar modernization is adding digitally controlled knitting, warping, and prototyping systems for rapid pattern development and real-time design sharing.

Shawmut Infinite serves automotive (including headliner fabrics), medical, filtration, military, protective apparel, hook-and-loop closure, and general apparel markets. Its customer base includes automotive and industrial designers who rely on rapid prototyping and digital production management.

