UPDATE companies SET description='Sigmatex was founded in 1986 and is headquartered in Cameron, South Carolina. For well over 30 years, the company has been a pioneer in the design, development, and manufacture of carbon fibre textiles for the composites industry.

The company produces a broad range of carbon fibre fabrics using what it describes as the widest array of conversion technologies available. Its product lines include 2D woven fabrics (plain, twill, satin, and complex designs), spread tow fabrics (sigmaST), multiaxial non-crimp fabrics (NCF), unidirectional fabrics with various stabilising methods, flat tow fabrics (sigmaFT), and recycled fabrics (sigmaRF) made from internal and customer production waste.

Sigmatex serves all industrial markets, with explicit mention of automotive, sporting goods, consumer electronics, and aerospace applications. The company is on the journey to AS9100D certification for aerospace supply.

Sigmatex emphasizes its unrivalled range of carbon fibre grades, including recycled materials, and customised textile solutions designed for performance. It has set public sustainability targets: a 25% reduction in energy consumption per linear meter of fabric by 2025, sourcing more than 50% of energy from renewables by 2025, zero waste to landfill by 2026, and a greater than 25% cut in transportation CO2 emissions by the end of 2024.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["2D woven fabrics", "Spread tow fabrics", "Multiaxial non-crimp fabrics (NCF)", "Unidirectional fabrics", "Flat tow fabrics", "Recycled fabrics", "Carbon fibre textile design and development", "Conversion technologies"], "industries": ["Composites", "Automotive", "Sporting goods", "Consumer electronics", "Aerospace"], "materials": ["Carbon fibre", "Recycled carbon fibre"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Widest array of conversion technologies for carbon fibre textiles", "Unrivalled range of carbon fibre grades including recycled materials", "Customised carbon textile solutions designed for performance", "Sustainability targets: 25% energy reduction per linear meter by 2025, >50% renewable energy by 2025, zero waste to landfill by 2026, >25% transport CO2 reduction by 2024"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1986 -> db", "Headquarters Cameron, South Carolina -> db", "Manufactures carbon fibre textiles -> /", "Produces 2D woven, spread tow, multiaxial NCF, unidirectional, flat tow, recycled fabrics -> /services", "Serves automotive, sporting goods, consumer electronics, aerospace -> /", "On the journey to AS9100D certification for aerospace -> /", "Sustainability commitments (energy, renewables, waste, CO2) -> /", "Languages supported (English, Chinese, Italian, Japanese, German, Spanish, French) -> /", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "WE PRODUCE ADVANCED COMPOSITE MATERIALS", "founded_year": "1986", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": ["English", "Chinese", "Italian", "Japanese", "German", "Spanish", "French"], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/sigmatex-uk/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sigmatex' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Signum, LLC operates from two North Dakota locations: an engineering hub in Fargo and a manufacturing facility in Richardton. The company was formed in 2019 as a joint venture between Amber Waves Electronics, founded in 2003 by Doug Hauck, and QED Embedded, founded in 2013 by Ed Schwind.

Its ISO 9001:2015, ISO 13485:2016, and ISO 27001:2022 certified facility in Richardton handles surface‑mount assembly, conformal coating, and prototyping through full‑scale production runs, supporting high‑mix, precision electronic manufacturing.

