UPDATE companies SET description='Six Robblees'' Inc. traces its roots to 1913 when three brothers—Jim, Bill, and Herb Robblee—founded J.A. Robblee & Co. in Tacoma, Washington. The firm began as a bicycle repair shop before transitioning to racing car wheel work after World War I. By 1920 a second location opened in Seattle, and in 1930 the company was renamed Six Robblees'' Inc. after Jim Robblee willed his share to his six remaining brothers. Today the business remains family-owned and is headquartered in Twin Falls, Idaho.

The company operates as a warehouse distributor of truck, trailer, and RV parts, as well as tire shop supplies and equipment. It stocks over 40,000 part numbers across 22 branches spanning eight states (Alaska, Montana, Oregon, Washington, Idaho, Wyoming, California, and others). The network grew through acquisitions such as Union Rubber Company, Motor Wheel and Parts, and several Alaska-based firms. The distributor offers online account management and credit terms to its customers.

Six Robblees'' serves the heavy-truck, light-truck, trailer, recreational vehicle, and tire-service sectors. The product range covers air brake components, axle and suspension parts, electrical wiring, exhaust components, fifth-wheel parts, hose assemblies, and a full line of tire service tools and TPMS accessories.

