UPDATE companies SET description='Smith Brothers of Berne traces its roots to 1926 in Berne, Indiana, where Homer Neiderhauser and the Dunbar Furniture Company established the Homer Manufacturing Company to produce lower-price point chairs that would supplement Dunbar’s high-end furniture lines. In 1936, Orv Smith and his brother Les Smith acquired a majority stake, renaming the business Smith Brothers Furniture Manufacturing Company and beginning a period of family-led growth that continued through 1960.

Today the company operates as a furniture manufacturer with a workforce of approximately 30 employees in Berne.

No further details on target sectors or client types are provided.

The business was founded to fill a gap in the market by offering affordable seating options alongside premium offerings, a positioning that the company cites as its founding purpose. The Smith brothers’ acquisition in 1936 set the stage for decades of independent operation in a region dominated by larger furniture makers.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Chair manufacturing", "Furniture manufacturing"], "industries": [], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Lower-price point chairs designed to complement high-end furniture lines", "Family-owned since the Smith brothers acquired majority control in 1936", "Continuous operation in Berne, Indiana since 1926"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1926 in Berne, Indiana -> db", "Founders Homer Neiderhauser, Orv Smith, Les Smith -> db", "Started as Homer Manufacturing Company, later Smith Brothers Furniture Manufacturing Company -> db", "Employee count 30 -> db", "Produces lower-price point chairs to supplement high-end furniture -> db", "Family ownership since 1936 -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "manufacturer of lower-price point chairs", "founded_year": "1926", "employee_count": "30", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='smith-brothers-of-berne-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='SMT Manufacturing Group LLC operates from Hallam, Pennsylvania, and was founded in 2001 by Mark Gingalewski, who serves as managing partner. The company describes itself as a small business focused on contract electronic assembly for commercial and military customers, with a mission to become the primary contract manufacturer of choice.

The facility specializes in fine-pitch surface mount assembly, through-hole assembly, and complete box-build integration, supported by automated optical and X-ray inspection, RoHS-compliant processing, and in-house programming of AVR, PIC, and development boards. The shop is structured for small-batch, quick-turn work, typically handling runs under 1,000 units with a two-week average turnaround.

Customers span commercial and military sectors, with the company highlighting its ability to manage both electrical design and test requirements. The staff includes IPC-certified instructors and adheres to IPC-610/620 Class 3 and J-STD-001 standards, supported by an ISO 9001:2015 quality system.

