UPDATE companies SET description='Solar Energy Services, LLC operates from Nixa, Missouri, serving the Southwest Missouri region since its founding in 2011. The family-owned business was established by master electrician Derek West and his wife Ashley; West brought over 17 years of solar industry experience to the venture.

The company designs and installs custom solar energy systems, including grid-tie arrays, off-grid solutions, battery backup storage, electric vehicle charging stations, and generator backup. Its technicians manage the full project lifecycle—from engineering and permitting through installation and ongoing maintenance—tailoring each system to the customer’s site and energy goals.

Customers range from homeowners and small businesses seeking lower utility bills to remote cabin owners and telecommunications sites requiring reliable off-grid power. The firm has also equipped water-heating systems and provided backup generation for residential and light-commercial clients across the region.

West’s master electrician license and Missouri state electrical contractor credential underpin the company’s emphasis on code-compliant, long-lasting installations built to perform for 25 years or more. The founders say they started the business to deliver dependable energy independence—whether for daily savings or catastrophic outage resilience—backed by hands-on technical support throughout the system’s life.', certifications=ARRAY['Master Electrician','Missouri State Electrical Contractor']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar PV system design", "Grid-tie solar installation", "Off-grid solar installation", "Battery backup system installation", "EV charger installation", "Generator installation", "Solar system maintenance", "Electrical contracting", "Permitting and engineering support"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Remote/off-grid power", "Telecommunications", "Water heating"], "materials": ["Solar photovoltaic modules", "Inverters", "Battery storage systems", "EV charging equipment", "Generators"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Master electrician founder with Missouri state electrical contractor license", "Family-owned and operated", "15+ years of experience in power supply and renewable energy solutions", "Full-service design, installation, and maintenance of solar, battery, EV charging, and generator systems", "Custom-engineered solutions for grid-tie, off-grid, and backup power applications"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2011 -> db", "Headquarters in Nixa, Missouri -> db", "Family-owned business -> /about-us", "Founders: Derek West (master electrician) and Ashley West -> /about-us", "Derek West has 17+ years solar industry experience -> /about-us", "Services: grid-tie, off-grid, battery backup, EV charging, generator -> / and /about-us", "Full project lifecycle: engineering, permitting, installation, maintenance -> /", "Customer types: homeowners, businesses, remote cabins, telecommunications, water heating -> /about-us", "Master Electrician / Missouri State Electrical Contractor license -> /", "Emphasis on 25+ year system performance -> /about-us", "15+ years experience in power supply and renewable energy -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Our team of experts will handle everything, from installation to maintenance", "founded_year": "2011", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='solar-energy-services-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Solar Guardians USA was founded in 2021 in Blackwood, New Jersey. The company operates as a solar repair and maintenance service provider for residential customers across New Jersey and southeastern Pennsylvania.

The company specializes in the service side of solar energy systems, offering panel removal and reinstallation for roof repairs, routine operation and maintenance, inverter repair and replacement, animal protection through critter guard installation, and consultation services including shading analysis and contract assessment. It does not install new systems but focuses on troubleshooting and restoring existing installations. The team works with a variety of racking components, inverters, and panel brands, and maintains two maintenance programs—one for newer installations and an extended program for systems over five years old.

Solar Guardians USA serves homeowners, solar financiers, leasing companies, and installation firms. It acts as a certified service provider for most large financiers and is an approved service contractor for brands such as SunPower and Sunova. The company also partners with multiple roofing contractors to coordinate roof repairs alongside solar system removal and reinstallation.

The business was built on the premise that solar system owners need dedicated service technicians rather than installers who prioritize new sales. It emphasizes its BBB accreditation, state electrical and home improvement licenses in New Jersey and Pennsylvania, and over 15 years of combined industry experience among its staff to differentiate itself in the market.', certifications=ARRAY['NJ Electrical License 34EB01091200','NJ Home Improvement Contractor (HIC) License 13VH10986500','PA Home Improvement Contractor (HIC) License PA156081']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar panel removal and reinstallation", "Solar operation and maintenance", "Solar panel replacement", "Solar inverter repair and replacement", "Solar manufacturer warranty assistance", "Animal protection and critter guard installation", "Solar consultation (shading analysis, contract assessment, home inspection)", "Roof leak inspections", "Roofing repairs (via partners)", "Maintenance Assurance Program for new installations", "Extended Maintenance Program for older systems", "Maintenance Assurance Program for installers", "Repair, service, and maintenance for leasing and finance companies"], "industries": ["Solar energy", "Residential solar", "Solar financing and leasing", "Roofing"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Focuses exclusively on solar service and repair, not new installations", "Certified service provider for most large solar financiers", "Approved service contractor for SunPower and Sunova", "BBB accredited with NJ and PA electrical and home improvement licenses", "Offers maintenance programs for both new and aging solar systems"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2021 in Blackwood, NJ -> db", "Services: solar panel removal/reinstallation, operation and repair, animal protection, consultation, maintenance programs -> /, /about-us, /services", "Certified service provider for most large financiers -> /, /about-us", "Approved service contractor for SunPower and Sunova -> /about-us", "BBB accredited -> /about-us", "NJ Electrical License 34EB01091200, NJ HIC 13VH10986500, PA HIC PA156081 -> /about-us", "Focuses solely on service side, not installation -> /services", "Partners with roofing contractors -> /, /about-us", "Offers Maintenance Assurance Program and Extended Maintenance Program -> /about-us, /services", "Serves homeowners, financiers, leasing companies, installers -> /, /about-us, /services"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Solar Guardians USA focuses solely on the service side of the business, meaning we are not installers. We are service technicians solving your problems and getting your system back up and running as quickly as possible.", "founded_year": "2021", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='solar-guardians-usa' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Solar Me was founded in 2014 in Jamesburg, New Jersey, as a small business with the goal of making sustainable energy more accessible to New Jersey residents and businesses. The company was built on the expertise of local solar consultants and homeowners, though the founder is not named in public materials.

The firm provides a full range of solar services including new system installations, diagnostics and repair, orphan system takeover, panel removal and decommissioning, critter and pest damage repair, and battery backup installation. It also offers commercial solar solutions for offices, retail spaces, and multifamily complexes, along with SREC management and system design. As of the latest figures, Solar Me has completed over 1,100 projects in New Jersey and installed more than 12 MW of solar capacity across New Jersey, Pennsylvania, and New York.

The company serves both residential and commercial customers. Residential work includes installations in towns such as Boonton, Rumson, Watchung, South Brunswick, Vineland, Bernardsville, and Hamilton. Commercial clients include office buildings, retail centers, and multifamily properties. Solar Me also acts as a long-term service partner for systems originally installed by other companies that have gone out of business.

Solar Me was started with the dream of creating a more renewable future and emphasizes honest answers, clean designs, and smart recommendations. The company highlights its Tesla Energy Certified Installer status and NABCEP certification as markers of technical competence, and it differentiates itself by taking over orphaned systems and restoring monitoring without requiring the original installer.', certifications=ARRAY['Tesla Energy Certified Installer','NABCEP (North American Board of Certified Energy Practitioners)']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar panel installation", "Solar system diagnostics and repair", "Orphan system takeover", "Panel removal and decommissioning", "Critter and pest damage repair", "Battery backup and storage installation", "Commercial solar installation", "SREC management", "Solar system design", "Solar monitoring restoration", "Inverter fault diagnosis", "Wiring repair", "Critter guard installation", "Roof replacement coordination", "System testing and production verification", "Tesla Powerwall installation", "Enphase microinverter installation", "SolarEdge inverter installation"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Multifamily", "Retail", "Office"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["Tesla Powerwall", "Hanwha Q CELLS solar panels", "LG solar panels (LG320N1C-G4)", "Panasonic solar panels", "Enphase microinverters", "SolarEdge inverters", "Q-PEAK ML-G10+ solar panels"], "volume": "12 MW installed capacity; 1,100+ completed projects", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Tesla Energy Certified Installer", "NABCEP certified", "Orphan system takeover and monitoring restoration", "Critter guard installation and pest damage repair", "Battery backup installation with Virtual Power Plant incentive assistance"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 2014 -> /about-us", "Headquarters in Jamesburg, New Jersey -> db", "Small business ownership -> /about-us", "Tesla Energy Certified Installer -> /", "NABCEP certified -> /about-us", "1,100+ completed projects in New Jersey -> /", "12 MW of solar capacity installed -> /", "Service area: NJ, PA, NY -> /", "Orphan system takeover service -> /", "Critter guard installation and pest damage repair -> /", "Battery backup installation with Virtual Power Plant incentives -> /", "Commercial solar for offices, retail, multifamily -> /", "Residential project examples in Boonton, Rumson, Watchung, South Brunswick, Vineland, Bernardsville, Hamilton -> /", "Brands worked with: Hanwha Q CELLS, LG, Panasonic, Enphase, SolarEdge, Tesla Powerwall -> /, /about-us"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Solar Me has been the trusted partner for expert solar service, repairs, and energy upgrades across NJ, PA, and NY. We help homeowners and businesses with diagnostics, critter damage protection, battery backup, removal, reinstallation, decommissioning, and complete system installations \u2014 including taking over orphaned systems when the original installer is no longer around.", "founded_year": "2014", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/solar-me-usa/"], "ownership_tags": ["Small business"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='solar-me' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Solar Power & Light, LLC (SP&L) was founded in 2010 in Miamisburg, Ohio, as a spin-off of the Inc. 5000-recognized parent company buyCASTINGS.com, whose management team had operated in the Ohio market since 2000. The company was established by Neil Chaudhry (CEO) and Greg Akers (Business Development Executive) to pioneer Power Purchase Agreements for municipal clients, winning the City of Cincinnati’s inaugural solar RFP in 2012.

SP&L delivers full-spectrum solar services: development (site assessment, PPA contracting, land acquisition, utility interconnection), engineering-procurement-construction (EPC) through SP&L Solar Installers, LLC, asset management (performance analytics, O&M, SREC brokerage), residential solar and consumer services (installation, battery storage, backup generators, financing), and a $300M+ funding engine (SP&L Money Solutions) plus $15M+ in federal and state R&D grants. To date, the firm has originated over 200 MW of PPA contracts, constructed more than 11 MW for public entities, and manages 14+ MW across 29 sites in Ohio, Kentucky, Pennsylvania, Illinois, and Minnesota.

The company serves commercial, industrial, educational, municipal, agricultural, nonprofit, and residential customers. Reference projects include a 500 kW installation for the City of Cincinnati, 55 kW and 80 kW systems for Wangler Ace Hardware and Ace Hardware in Greenville, a 99.5 kW array for Billenstein Family Farm, a PPA for the City of Franklin’s water treatment plant, and a $1.5 million project for Ansonia Local Schools delivering over $50,000 in annual savings.

SP&L differentiates itself through its proprietary Integrated Development Teaming™ (IDT) methodology launched in 2012, distributed inverter architecture for superior low-light harvesting, automated wire-harness manufacturing adapted from automotive production, and early adoption of 1,000-volt DC design to lower balance-of-system costs. As a federal contractor leveraging shared affiliate infrastructure, the firm emphasizes enduring value, innovative technology, and efficient solutions that reduce levelized cost of energy for investors and host sites.', certifications=ARRAY['Avetta Compliance','Green Energy Certified','Inc. 5000 Honoree','EnergySage']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar PV system design and engineering", "Turnkey solar installation (rooftop, carport, ground-mount)", "Battery storage installation, diagnostics, and monitoring", "Orphaned system support (troubleshooting, repairs, maintenance for any brand)", "Detach and reset for re-roofing", "Operations & maintenance (O&M) and real-time monitoring", "Performance analytics and SREC brokerage", "PPA origination, contracting, and lease management", "Site assessment, land acquisition, utility interconnection pre-assessment", "AHJ engagement and permitting", "Residential solar and consumer financing", "Commercial peak demand shaving", "USDA REAP grant assistance for agricultural projects", "SP&L Money Solutions project financing", "Research & development (DOE SunShot, STEM-integrated solar education)"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Industrial", "Agricultural", "Municipal", "Nonprofit", "Educational (schools)", "Utility-scale"], "materials": ["Tier 1 solar panels (1000V)", "Distributed inverters", "Automated wire harnesses", "Battery storage systems", "Backup generators"], "equipment": [], "volume": "200+ MW PPA originated; 11+ MW constructed for public entities; 14+ MW under management", "lead_time": "Proposal within one business day", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Proprietary Integrated Development Teaming\u2122 (IDT) methodology", "Distributed inverter architecture for superior low-light harvesting", "Automated wire-harness manufacturing adapted from automotive/electronics", "Early adoption of 1,000-volt DC design to cut balance-of-system cost", "$300M+ funding engine connecting projects with institutional financing"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2010 in Miamisburg, Ohio -> /about", "Spin-off of buyCASTINGS.com (Inc. 5000 parent) -> /about", "Founders Neil Chaudhry (CEO) and Greg Akers -> /about", "Management team operating in Ohio since 2000 -> /about", "Pioneered PPAs for municipal market, won City of Cincinnati RFP 2012 -> /about", "Launched Integrated Development Teaming\u2122 (IDT) methodology 2012 -> /about", "200+ MW PPA originated -> /about", "11+ MW constructed for public entities -> /about", "14+ MW under management across 29 sites -> /about", "5 states: OH, KY, PA, IL, MN -> /about", "$300M+ funding engine (SP&L Money Solutions) -> /about", "$15M+ federal/state R&D grants, DOE SunShot Award with Stanford Research Institute -> /about", "Distributed inverter architecture, automated wire-harness manufacturing, 1000V design -> /about", "Federal contractor leveraging shared affiliate infrastructure -> /about", "Services: solar installation, battery storage, orphaned system support, detach & reset, O&M, development -> /services", "Sectors served: residential, commercial, agricultural, municipal, nonprofits -> /services", "Reference projects: City of Cincinnati 500kW, Wangler Ace Hardware 55kW, Ace Hardware Greenville 80kW, Billenstein Family Farm 99.5kW, City of Franklin water treatment PPA, Ansonia Local Schools $1.5M -> / and /about", "Certifications: Avetta Compliance, Green Energy Certified, Inc. 5000 Honoree, EnergySage -> /", "Proposal turnaround within one business day -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "From site identification to 20-year asset management, SP&L handles ever