UPDATE companies SET description='The business grew from Canavan’s decade of experience installing over a thousand solar PV and solar thermal systems across the Cape, Islands, and southeastern Massachusetts.

The company provides full‑service solar installation for residential and commercial customers, including system design, permitting, installation, battery storage, EV charger installation, and ongoing maintenance and repair. They also offer electrical services and partner with Cape Cod Heat Pumps for integrated heat‑pump solutions. The team reports more than 1,100 completed installations and over 42,000 megawatt‑hours of power generated since inception.

Solar Rising serves homeowners and businesses throughout Cape Cod and all of Massachusetts. Their residential clients include homeowners seeking rooftop PV, battery backup, and EV charging; commercial clients range from small businesses to larger facilities looking to offset electricity costs. The company also works with customers needing electrical upgrades, critter guard installation, and system removal for roof replacement.

The company emphasizes attention to detail, lasting customer relationships, and sustainability as core differentiators.', certifications=ARRAY['NABCEP Certified Photovoltaic Installer','Massachusetts Master Electrician License','Massachusetts Journeyman Electrician License','Massachusetts Construction Supervisor License','Massachusetts Hoisting Engineer License']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Residential solar PV design and installation", "Commercial solar PV design and installation", "Battery storage system installation", "EV charger installation", "Electrical services and upgrades", "Solar system maintenance and repair", "System removal and reinstallation for roof replacement", "Critter guard installation", "Solar thermal (SDHW) installation", "Permitting and incentive paperwork management"], "industries": ["Residential", "Commercial", "Electrical contracting", "Renewable energy", "Energy storage", "EV charging infrastructure"], "materials": ["Solar photovoltaic modules (e.g., SunPower)", "Inverters", "Battery storage systems", "EV charging stations", "Solar thermal collectors"], "equipment": [], "volume": "Over 1,100 completed installations; 42,000+ MWh generated", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Over 1,100 completed solar installations across Cape Cod and Massachusetts", "Team holds multiple NABCEP certifications and state licenses (Master Electrician, Construction Supervisor, Hoisting Engineer)", "Full\u2011service offering: solar PV, battery storage, EV chargers, electrical work, and maintenance under one roof", "Partnership with Cape Cod Heat Pumps for integrated heat\u2011pump and solar solutions", "Emphasis on long\u2011term customer relationships and sustainability as core business values"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2008 -> db", "Headquarters Mashpee, MA -> db", "Founder Ben Canavan, NABCEP certified, over 1,000 installations -> description, /about", "Team members Angela Hemmila, Neal Holmgren, Chris Peterson with NABCEP and state licenses -> /about", "Services: residential/commercial solar, battery storage, EV chargers, electrical, maintenance -> /", "Stats: 1,100+ installations, 42,000+ MWh generated -> /", "Partnership with Cape Cod Heat Pumps -> /", "Company type: full-service solar installation company -> /", "Licenses: Master Electrician #22750-A, Construction Supervisor licenses, Hoisting Engineer -> /about", "NABCEP certification numbers for each team member -> /about"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Solar Rising is a Cape Cod based full service solar installation company", "founded_year": "2008", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='solar-rising' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Solar Technology Alabama is based in Eva, Alabama. The company was founded in 2008 by Ron Holland, a Mississippi State University electrical engineering graduate who spent 20 years as a power distribution engineer at Southern Company. His concern over grid vulnerability and interest in self‑sufficiency led him to start the business; he later built the Alabama Solar Technology Center and has lived off‑grid since 2011.

The firm designs and installs custom off‑grid and stand‑alone solar power systems, including solar water heating, solar water pumping, and battery backup systems. Services cover full installation, system sizing, permitting, plumbing adjustments, commissioning, and a paid consultation offering for system optimization. Operations span from Montgomery to southern Middle Tennessee.

Customers are homeowners, cabin owners, and businesses seeking energy independence in North Alabama. Some clients are fully off‑grid, while others keep grid connection but install off‑grid systems for essential loads. The company explicitly does not accept residential grid‑tie projects.

The company says its differentiator is firsthand off‑grid living experience since 2011, climate‑specific designs that account for Alabama’s hard freezes, and a focus on energy security through storage rather than grid cooperation. Consultation services aim to educate customers on system limits and capabilities.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Off\u2011grid system installation", "Solar water heating installation", "Solar water pumping installation", "Battery backup design", "Renewable energy system design", "Paid consultation service", "System sizing and design", "Permitting and plumbing adjustments", "System testing and walkthrough"], "industries": ["Renewable Energy", "Solar Energy", "Off\u2011grid Power Systems", "Solar Water Heating", "Solar Water Pumping"], "materials": ["Solar panels", "Batteries", "Grid\u2011independent inverters", "Insulated storage tanks", "Solar thermal collectors", "Pumps"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Custom\u2011designed off\u2011grid and stand\u2011alone power systems", "Founder has lived off\u2011grid since 2011", "No grid\u2011tie projects; pure off\u2011grid approach with battery storage", "Climate\u2011specific system design for North Alabama freeze risks", "Paid consultation for system optimization and customer education"], "facts_used": ["Founder Ron Holland, electrical engineer, 20 years at Southern Company -> db", "Founded 2008 -> /", "Lived off-grid since 2011 -> /", "Alabama Solar Technology Center in Eva, AL -> /", "Services: off-grid installation, solar water heating, solar water pumping, battery backup, consultation -> /", "Service area Montgomery to southern Middle Tennessee -> /", "No residential grid-tie projects -> /", "Climate-specific design for North Alabama freezes -> /about-us", "System types: passive, active, closed-loop solar water heating -> /about-us", "Cost ranges and payback figures for solar water heating -> /about-us", "YouTube channel idosolar -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Solar Tech provides custom-designed systems and installation of off-grid and stand-alone power systems", "founded_year": "2008", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='solar-technology-alabama' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Solar Topps was founded in 2009 in Phoenix, Arizona, as a family-owned solar and battery installation company. The business began with a focus on providing premium solar energy solutions at the lowest prices, serving homeowners and businesses across Arizona.

The company designs, engineers, installs, and services rooftop, ground-mount, and shade-structure solar systems, along with battery backup and EV charging solutions. All design, engineering, installation, and support are performed in-house by trained professionals—no subcontractors are used. Solar Topps stocks materials locally to enable quick installations and rapid service response, often dispatching technicians within hours. Since inception, the firm has installed over 3.15 million solar panels, integrated more than 1,200 battery backup systems, and helped over 25,000 homeowners go solar, delivering a cumulative $950 million in utility-bill savings.

Solar Topps serves residential and commercial customers throughout Arizona. Its client base includes thousands of homeowners—such as the Heusinkveld, Edlund, Borino, and Singh families—and businesses seeking energy independence. The company maintains working relationships with utilities like APS, city permitting offices, and HOAs to streamline approvals and interconnections.

The company says it was started to prioritize engineering quality, long-term risk mitigation, and service reality—areas where it claims many installers fall short. Its family-owned structure means it answers to customers rather than investors, and its in-house model ensures accountability from design through long-term support. Solar Topps holds an A+ BBB rating and was named EnergySage 2026 Local Installer of the Year in Arizona.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar PV system design and engineering", "Rooftop solar installation", "Ground-mount solar installation", "Shade structure solar installation", "Battery backup system installation", "EV charging station installation", "Solar panel removal and reinstallation", "Solar panel removal and disposal/recycling", "Existing system expansion (adding panels)", "Solar panel replacement", "System monitoring and maintenance", "Permitting and utility interconnection coordination", "Project management", "In-house installation (no subcontractors)", "Rapid service dispatch"], "industries": ["Residential solar", "Commercial solar", "Battery energy storage", "EV charging infrastructure"], "materials": ["Solar panels", "FranklinWH batteries", "Enphase microinverters", "EV chargers"], "equipment": ["FranklinWH battery systems", "Enphase microinverters and products"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Service dispatch within hours; installations in under 2 months", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house engineering, installation, and service teams (no subcontractors)", "Locally stocked materials for quick installs and rapid service response", "Proactive utility, permitting, and HOA relationships", "Family-owned with direct customer accountability", "Engineering-focused, performance-driven system design"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2009 in Phoenix, Arizona -> db", "Family-owned, locally owned -> /about-us", "No subcontractors, in-house teams -> /about-us", "3.15+ million panels installed -> /", "2.25 million panels installed (alternate figure) -> /about-us", "30k+ happy customers -> /", "1,200 battery backup systems integrated -> /about-us", "25,000 homeowners helped go solar -> /about-us", "$950 million saved on utility bills -> /about-us", "$4.1 billion property value raised -> /about-us", "A+ BBB rated -> /", "EnergySage 2026 Local Installer of the Year Arizona -> /about-us", "Works with APS, city permitting offices, HOAs -> /about-us", "FranklinWH batteries, Enphase products -> /, /about-us", "Services: new installs, add-ons, battery-only, removal/reinstall, removal/discard, panel replacement, expansion -> /services", "Service dispatch within hours -> /about-us", "90-panel system up in <2 months -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "We are a highly accredited construction engineering firm that specializes in designing, installing, and servicing rooftop, ground mount, and shade structure solar systems for homes and businesses.", "founded_year": "2009", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='solar-topps' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='SolarReviews operates from Denver, Colorado, where it was founded in 2013 by Australian entrepreneurs Andy Sendy and Vassie Fitzgerald. The company, owned by Solar Investments Inc., began after the co-founders recognized a disconnect between American consumers and solar installers, setting out to provide resources for researching solar panels, connecting with installers, and getting solar on roofs.

The platform provides a solar cost and savings calculator that requires only a zip code and electricity bill, an unbiased consumer review platform covering U.S. solar companies and equipment, and a matching service that connects homeowners with up to four local installers. The editorial team, with more than 50 years of combined solar industry experience, produces expert rankings and articles cited by outlets such as NPR, CNBC, and Bloomberg. SolarReviews reports having assisted over 1.6 million consumers with their solar journeys.

The service serves two primary audiences: homeowners evaluating residential solar options and solar installation companies seeking qualified leads. Installers can register to receive consumer inquiries filtered by service categories ranging from grid-tied residential systems to battery storage and off-grid installations. The company partners with industry organizations including SEIA, CALSSA, NABCEP, and Solar Energy International.

SolarReviews emphasizes trust, expertise, and privacy as differentiators. Its calculator does not collect personal information, consumers control how many installers contact them, and data can be removed on request. The company states that none of its journalists or editors has a financial relationship with any solar manufacturer, distributor, or installer, and that it drops partners who sell consumer data.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Solar cost and savings calculator", "Unbiased consumer review platform for solar companies and equipment", "Installer matching and lead generation (1\u20134 installers per consumer)", "Editorial content and expert rankings for solar products", "Privacy-controlled consumer data handling"], "industries": ["Residential solar", "Solar installation", "Solar equipment"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Calculator requires only zip code and electric bill, no personal information", "Consumers choose 1\u20134 installers to be contacted by; data never sold beyond that", "Consumer data removable on request", "Editorial independence: no financial ties to solar manufacturers or installers", "Partners dropped if they sell consumer data"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2013 -> db", "Headquarters Denver, Colorado -> db", "Co-founders Andy Sendy and Vassie Fitzgerald -> /about-us", "Owner Solar Investments Inc. -> /about-us", "Helped over 1.6 million consumers -> /about-us", "Editorial team 50+ years combined experience -> /about-us", "Partners: SEIA, CALSSA, NABCEP, Solar Energy International -> /about-us", "Cited by NPR, CNBC, Bloomberg -> /about-us", "Calculator requires only zip code and electric bill -> /about-us", "Consumers choose 1-4 installers -> /about-us", "Data removable on request -> /about-us", "No financial relationships with solar companies -> /about-us", "Australian co-founders -> /about-us", "Mission to make going solar easy -> /about-us", "Services categories for installers -> /services"], "company_type": "Other", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "At its core, SolarReviews is a source for consumers and installers to connect, making going solar as easy as possible.", "founded_year": "2013", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='solarreviews' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Solid Stone Fabrics was founded in 2003 by David L. Stone Jr. in Martinsville, Virginia, a city once known as the "Sweatshirt Capital of the World." Stone launched the business from his garage, determined to keep textile manufacturing alive in a region that had seen major plant closures. The company moved from a local business incubator to an 18,000-square-foot facility before settling in its current 82,000-square-foot building in 2015.

The operation combines wholesale fabric distribution with a full-service custom printing and cut-and-sew facility. The warehouse stocks more than 90,000 yards of performance, specialty, and novelty fabrics—including stretch, hologram, sequin, velvet, and eco-friendly lines. In-house printing capabilities cover dye sublimation, acid dye for nylon, UV, and latex processes, while a laser cutting department and industrial sewing team produce flags, banners, marching-band uniforms, and home‑décor items such as wallpaper, desk mats, and canvas art.

Customers span the performance‑arts, costume, entertainment, fashion, and swimwear markets, as well as dance and team‑spirit groups, marching bands, theme parks, and interior‑design professionals. The company also supplies home‑décor retailers with finished goods ranging from wall murals to acrylic accessories.

Stone’s original goal was to bring textile printing back to the United States, eliminating the high minimums, long lead times, and questionable chemical processes associated with overseas production. The firm emphasizes low minimums—one yard for stock fabrics, five yards for custom prints—quick turnaround, and clean, domestically produced textiles.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Wholesale fabric distribution", "Custom fabric printing (dye sublimation)", "Custom fabric printing (acid dye for nylon)", "UV printing", "Latex printing", "Laser fabric cutting", "Industrial sewing (flags, banners, uniforms)", "Home d\u00e9cor manufacturing (wallpaper, desk mats, canvas art, etc.)", "Graphic design services", "Custom fabric sourcing and blending"], "industries": ["Performance arts", "Costume", "Entertainment", "Fashion", "Swimwear", "Dance", "Team/spirit", "Active apparel", "Marching band", "Theme parks", "Home d\u00e9cor", "Interior design"], "materials": ["Stretch fabrics", "Hologram fabrics", "Sequin fabrics", "Velvet fabrics", "Eco-friendly fabrics", "Nylon/Lycra", "Polyester/Spandex", "Glitter fabrics", "Tulle and mesh", "Polyester base fabrics", "Nylon base fabrics", "Rigid substrates (paper, acrylic, wood, glass, vinyl, leather, foam core, plastics, banners, canvas, metal)"], "equipment": ["UV printer", "Laser cutting equipment", "Industrial sewing machines", "Sublimation printing equipment", "Acid dye printing equipment", "Latex printing equipment"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Quick turnaround times for custom printing", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["1-yard minimum on stock fabrics", "5-yard minimum on custom printed fabrics", "Quick turnaround on custom printing", "Made-in-USA textile printing", "Clean sublimation and direct-to-textile processes"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2003 by David L. Stone Jr. in Martinsville, VA -> /about", "Started in garage, moved to incubator, then 18,000 sq ft, then 82,000 sq ft in 2015 -> /about", "Warehouse stocks over 90,000 yards of fabric -> /about", "Printing processes: dye sublimation, acid dye, UV, latex -> /services", "Laser cutting and industrial sewing for flags, banners, uniforms -> /services", "Home d\u00e9cor manufacturing: wallpaper, desk mats, canvas art, etc. -> /services", "Industries served: performance arts, costume, entertainment, fashion, swimwear, dance, team/spirit, marching band, theme parks, home d\u00e9cor, interior design -> /about, /services", "Minimums: 1 yard stock, 5 yards custom printed -> /, /services", "Mission: bring textile printing back to USA, low minimums, quick turnaround, clean processes -> /about", "Equipment: UV printer, laser cutting, industrial sewing, sublimation/acid dye/latex printing equipment -> /services", "Materials: stretch, hologram, sequin, velvet, eco-friendly, nylon/lycra, polyester/spandex, glitter, tulle, mesh, polyester/nylon base fabrics, rigid substrates -> /, /about, /services"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Solid Stone Fabrics manufactures and distributes stretch fabrics for dance, team/spirit, costume, active apparel, swimwear, and many other markets.", "founded_year": "2003", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "1 yard for stock fabrics; 5 yards for custom printed fabric", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='solid-stone-fabrics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Sons of Sawdust Supply operates from Nashville, Tennessee, tracing its roots to 1926. The woodworking business began as a reclamation and fabrication shop focused on giving new life to aged lumber, though the founding family or individuals are not named in available records.

The company mills and sells reclaimed wood at a flat rate of $8 per board foot, offering hand-hewn beams sourced from log cabins and custom-milled lath for decorative applications. Its workshop produces made-to-order farm tables, furniture pieces, and full-scale build-outs for bars, restaurants, and hotels. A subscription service called Box of Drops delivers curated reclaimed wood assortments to repeat customers.

Its portfolio includes commercial installations for Nashville-area hospitality venues and custom furniture for private homes.

The business emphasizes the transformation of forgotten cabins and historic structures into functional, sustainable design elements, positioning reclaimed wood as both a material and a narrative for modern spaces.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Reclaimed wood milling and sales", "Custom farm table fabrication", "Custom furniture manufacturing", "Commercial hospitality build-out construction", "Hand-hewn beam production", "Decorative lath art fabrication", "Subscription box fulfillment (Box of Drops)"], "industries": ["Interior design", "Hospitality (bars, restaurants, hotels)", "Residential construction", "Commercial construction", "Retail lumber"], "materials": ["Reclaimed wood", "Hand-hewn timber", "Lath"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Reclaimed wood sold at $8 per board foot", "Hand-hewn beams salvaged from log cabins", "Full-service commercial and hospitality build-outs (bars, restaurants, hotels)", "Box of Drops subscription service for curated reclaimed wood", "Custom farm table and furniture manufacturing"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1926 -> db", "Headquarters Nashville, Tennessee -> db", "Sells reclaimed wood at $8 per board foot -> /", "Offers hand-hewn beams from log cabins -> /", "Builds custom farm tables and furniture -> /", "Provides commercial and hospitality build-outs for bars, restaurants, hotels -> /", "Operates Box of Drops subscription service -> /", "Produces Batman Building Reclaimed Lath Art -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "woodworking business located in Nashville, TN that specializes in selling reclaimed wood, building custom farm tables and furniture, and transforming entire spaces with reclaimed wood", "founded_year": "1926", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='sons-of-sa